    "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::locale_load_failures_swallowed_dead_checks": {
      "issue_id": "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::locale_load_failures_swallowed_dead_checks",
      "kind": "permanent",
      "reason": null,
      "note": "defer-to-followup-pr/error-contract - the proposed fix makes a missing or malformed packaged base YAML raise instead of degrading to {}, which turns a condition a WeeWX service currently tolerates into a hard startup failure of the whole weather station. That is a risk change, not a defect fix, and this cycle's split rule keeps only behaviour-correcting fixes in the bugfix PR. It needs its own PR where the new failure mode is the headline rather than a footnote under four unrelated bug fixes. The finding is NOT dropped: the contradiction it names is real - locale_loader.load_yaml returns {} on FileNotFoundError and yaml.YAMLError while the utils getters at lines 39-40, 47-48 and 55-56 advertise a RuntimeError that can therefore never fire - and the follow-up PR must settle it in one direction (raise for the packaged base, or delete the dead RuntimeError guards and document degradation as intended).",
      "attestation": "I have reviewed this triage skip against the code and I am not gaming the score by suppressing a real defect.",
      "created_at": "2026-11-10T11:42:10+00:00",
      "review_after": null,
      "skipped_at_scan": 2
    },
