      "action_steps": [
        {
          "title": "Add the failing battery fan-out regression test",
          "detail": "Create tests/test_preprocessor.py -- no such file exists today; tests/ holds ten modules and none of them touches src/weewx_ha/preprocessor.py. Assert, for input bitmaps 0, 1 and 255, that every one of the eight TX_BATTERY_STATUS_FIELDS values is exactly 0 or 1; that bitmap 255 makes all eight report 1 (measured current output is batteryStatusISS=1 then 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, so seven of the eight fail today); and that bitmap 0 makes all eight 0. Separately assert a None txBatteryStatus is tolerated: src/weewx_ha/preprocessor.py:35 currently raises TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for &: 'NoneType' and 'int' BEFORE the del at :36 runs, so the key survives and the entire packet is discarded by preprocessor_complete's handler at src/weewx_ha/controller.py:286. Assert the txBatteryStatus key is removed in every case including the None case. Record the failures with `pipenv run pytest tests/test_preprocessor.py` BEFORE editing the module: `pipenv run pytest --cov=weewx_ha --cov-report=term-missing` puts src/weewx_ha/preprocessor.py at 32% with lines 25 and 29-37 unexecuted, which is why this shipped.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::battery_bitmap_payload_mismatch",
            "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::none_txbattery_typeerror"
          ],
          "done": true
        },
        {
          "title": "Fix process_packet and strip the file's no-op scaffolding",
          "detail": "One edit to src/weewx_ha/preprocessor.py. (a) Replace `txBatteryStatus & (1 << i)` at :35 with `(tx_battery_status >> i) & 1` -- verified over all 256 possible bitmaps that this yields only 0 or 1 for all eight fields, matching payload_off: 0 / payload_on: 1 as declared at src/weewx_ha/locales/sensors.yaml:95-103 (batteryStatusChannel, which batteryStatusChannel1..7 reach through the numeric-suffix fallback at src/weewx_ha/utils.py:150-157) and :105-113 (batteryStatusISS). SCOPE CORRECTION to the item text: channels 1 through 7 are broken -- 7 of the 8 fields, not channels 2-7; only batteryStatusISS on bit 0 works today because 1 << 0 == 1. (b) Skip the fan-out loop when packet['txBatteryStatus'] is None while STILL executing `del packet['txBatteryStatus']` at :36 -- today the TypeError fires first, so the key is left behind. (c) Rename the camelCase local at :32 to tx_battery_status. (d) Delete the pass-only __init__ at :23-25 and the two content-free logger.debug calls at :29 and :31.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::battery_bitmap_payload_mismatch",
            "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::none_txbattery_typeerror",
            "review::.::holistic::naming_quality::camelcase_local_in_preprocessor",
            "review::.::holistic::ai_generated_debt::noop_preprocessor_init",
            "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::preprocessor_noop_init_and_unused_lambda_arg"
          ],
          "done": true
        }
      ]
    },
    "controller-init-lifecycle-contract": {
      "name": "controller-init-lifecycle-contract",
      "description": "Make Controller construction and teardown consistent in src/weewx_ha/controller.py: on a rejected configuration initialise the attributes shutDown dereferences instead of returning half-built, construct both publishers before the MQTT loop starts so the two getattr probes can be deleted, and tidy the error reporting on that path in controller.py and models/extension_config.py.",
      "issue_ids": [
        "review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::lifecycle_ordering_guards",
        "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::shutdown_after_failed_init",
        "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::controller_partial_construction",
        "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::controller_partial_init_on_config_error",
        "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::half_constructed_controller",
        "review::.::holistic::type_safety::controller_attrs_may_be_missing",
        "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::minor_error_context_inconsistencies"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-11-10T11:44:27+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-10T12:18:30+00:00",
      "auto": false,
      "cluster_key": "",
      "action": null,
      "action_type": "manual_fix",
      "execution_policy": "planned_only",
      "execution_status": "active",
      "user_modified": true,
      "priority": 2,
      "action_steps": [
        {
          "title": "Add the failing shutDown-after-rejected-config regression test",
          "detail": "Add the test to tests/test_mqtt_startup.py, which already carries the Controller harness (its mqtt_client fixture at :44-52 builds one via Controller.__new__ with paho patched through patch.object(mqtt, 'Client')). Here construct a REAL Controller(engine, config_dict) whose HomeAssistant stanza is invalid -- an unknown key suffices, since extra='forbid' is set at src/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py:19 -- then call shutDown() and assert AttributeError today, and no publish call after the fix. Verified in src/weewx_ha/controller.py: the `return` at :109 leaves self.config (:101), availability_topic (:127), mqtt_client (:128), executor (:131), packet_preprocessor (:134), config_publisher (:137) and state_publisher (:147) all unassigned, and shutDown dereferences self.mqtt_client at :480. `pipenv run pytest --cov=weewx_ha --cov-report=term-missing` shows lines 96-156 and 477-491 unexecuted. Record the failure first.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::shutdown_after_failed_init",
            "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::controller_partial_construction",
            "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::half_constructed_controller"
          ],
          "done": true
        },
        {
          "title": "Initialise the disabled Controller and make shutDown a no-op without a client",
          "detail": "Before the `return` at src/weewx_ha/controller.py:109, assign an explicit disabled flag plus safe defaults for every attribute the lifecycle methods read, so the class has ONE declared attribute set in both outcomes instead of two shapes. NAME CORRECTION to the organize text: the attribute is `packet_preprocessor` (assigned at :134), not `preprocessor`, and `self.config` (:101) belongs in the list too, because on_mqtt_connect reads self.config.discovery_topic_prefix at :211 and on_mqtt_message at :242. The full set is config, availability_topic (:127), mqtt_client (:128), executor (:131), packet_preprocessor (:134), config_publisher (:137), state_publisher (:147). Make shutDown return early when there is no client, ahead of the publish at :480. Add the missing exc_info=True to the logger.error at :487 -- verified the only `except` handler in the file without it, since :105, :266, :274, :286 and :414 all carry it. TYPE NOTE from the sense-check: the defaults must not fight mypy. mqtt_client is annotated `mqtt.Client` at :128, so widen the annotations of the attributes that can now be None (mqtt_client, config, executor, packet_preprocessor, config_publisher, state_publisher) to `X | None`, and keep the file mypy-clean against its current baseline of exactly one error (src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py:8). DO NOT touch loop_start() at :198 or the comment block at :186-197: the step that moved it is deferred, so that rationale stays true and tests/test_mqtt_startup.py:55-60 keeps passing. The two getattr probes at :216 and :244 also STAY, since they go with the deferred step.",
          "effort": "medium",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::shutdown_after_failed_init",
            "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::controller_partial_construction",
            "review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::half_constructed_controller",
            "review::.::holistic::type_safety::controller_attrs_may_be_missing",
            "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::controller_partial_init_on_config_error"
          ],
          "done": true
        },
        {
          "title": "Stop double-reporting the configuration ValidationError",
          "detail": "src/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py:65 logs `Configuration validation error: {e}` and src/weewx_ha/controller.py:105-108 logs the same failure again with exc_info=True. Keep the controller's one, which carries the 'Extension will not be loaded.' consequence, and delete the logger.error at extension_config.py:65 (its `logger` at :13 then has no remaining user in the file, so drop the logging import at :4 as well if nothing else uses it). Change `raise e` at extension_config.py:66 to a bare `raise` so the original traceback survives. Ordering constraint to honour: coverage-gaps-controller-and-catalogue step 1 asserts exactly one log on this path, so land this step before that test is written.",
          "effort": "trivial",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::error_consistency::minor_error_context_inconsistencies"
          ],
          "done": true
        }
      ]
    },
    "locale-cache-invalidation": {
      "name": "locale-cache-invalidation",
      "description": "Give src/weewx_ha/utils.py a single configure(language, overrides) entry point that sets the locale_loader state and clears all four lazy caches, call it from the Controller in place of the two bare setters, and only then centralise the test reset fixture in tests/conftest.py.",
      "issue_ids": [
        "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::locale_state_cache_not_invalidated",
        "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::language_setter_ignored_after_cache",
        "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::global_language_state_coordinates_modules",
        "review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::implicit_global_locale_state",
        "review::.::holistic::abstraction_fitness::utils_global_lazy_caches",
        "review::.::holistic::test_strategy::duplicated_locale_reset_fixture"
      ],
      "created_at": "2026-11-10T11:44:27+00:00",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-10T12:17:37+00:00",
      "auto": false,
      "cluster_key": "",
      "action": null,
      "action_type": "manual_fix",
      "execution_policy": "planned_only",
      "execution_status": "done",
      "user_modified": true,
      "priority": 3,
      "action_steps": [
        {
          "title": "Add the failing locale-setter effectiveness test",
          "detail": "Add the test to tests/test_locale_overrides.py. Call a utils getter first to populate the cache (get_sensors_yaml() or get_key_config_dict()), THEN call set_language('de') and assert the next src/weewx_ha/utils.py lookup returns the German name; repeat the same shape with set_config_overrides. Verified: set_language (src/weewx_ha/locale_loader.py:70-81) and set_config_overrides (:96-109) only assign the module globals _current_language (:15) and _config_overrides (:18), which load_yaml reads at :151 and :199, while src/weewx_ha/utils.py holds four independent caches -- _ENUM_MAPS, _UNIT_METADATA and _SENSORS_YAML (:20-22) plus _KEY_CONFIG (:254) -- that nothing ever clears, so each setter is silently inert after the first getter call. The existing suite hides this because all six reset_locale_state fixtures only ever set the language back to None. Record the failure first.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::language_setter_ignored_after_cache",
            "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::locale_state_cache_not_invalidated"
          ],
          "done": true
        },
        {
          "title": "Invalidate the utils caches from the existing locale setters",
          "detail": "SCOPE REDUCED by the sense-check value pass: do NOT add a public utils.configure(language, overrides) and do NOT rewrite the Controller call sites. A new public entry point is more than the defect needs and is itself an API change. Instead add one private reset in src/weewx_ha/utils.py that sets all four caches back to None -- _ENUM_MAPS, _UNIT_METADATA and _SENSORS_YAML (declared at src/weewx_ha/utils.py:20-22, populated by _ensure_loaded at :25-33) plus _KEY_CONFIG (:254, read by get_key_config_dict at :257-262) -- and call it from inside the two existing setters, set_language at src/weewx_ha/locale_loader.py:70 and set_config_overrides at :96. The Controller block at src/weewx_ha/controller.py:114-125 then needs NO edit at all, and the import at :24 stays used, which also removes the F401 cascade the sense-check flagged. Mind the direction of the dependency: locale_loader must not import utils at module scope, so do the import inside the setter bodies or have utils register a callback at import time; verify no cycle with pipenv run python -c 'import weewx_ha'. Two reviewer suggestions stay REJECTED: functools.cache on the getters, which hides the caches behind a decorator and makes the inertness harder to see, and the injected LocaleCatalog redesign, which is defer-to-followup-pr/module-decomposition work.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::locale_state_cache_not_invalidated",
            "review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::language_setter_ignored_after_cache",
            "review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::global_language_state_coordinates_modules",
            "review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::implicit_global_locale_state",
            "review::.::holistic::abstraction_fitness::utils_global_lazy_caches"
          ],
          "done": true
        },
        {
          "title": "Move reset_locale_state into conftest.py as one autouse fixture",
          "detail": "Do this only AFTER the step above lands -- the ordering is load-bearing. Verified: all six copies are byte-identical and only call set_language(None)/set_config_overrides(None), so today none of them can reach _KEY_CONFIG, _SENSORS_YAML, _UNIT_METADATA or _ENUM_MAPS in src/weewx_ha/utils.py:20-22 and :254, and centralising first would centralise a false guarantee. The six definitions are tests/test_locale_de.py:24, tests/test_locale_overrides.py:21, tests/test_hardening.py:12, tests/test_discovery_race.py:32, tests/test_publish.py:19 and tests/test_unit_groups.py:68. Replace them with ONE autouse fixture in tests/conftest.py -- which today has no fixtures at all, only pytest_addoption, pytest_configure and pytest_collection_modifyitems -- calling set_language(None) and set_config_overrides(None) before and after each test, which now genuinely clears the caches. COUNT CORRECTION measured by the sense-check: 19 test functions plus the publisher fixture at tests/test_discovery_race.py:42 lose the parameter, not 22. CASCADE the sense-check found: set_language and set_config_overrides then become unused imports in tests/test_hardening.py:7, tests/test_discovery_race.py:25, tests/test_publish.py:12 and tests/test_unit_groups.py:25, so drop them there or flake8 F401 fires in pre-commit; keep _deep_merge in test_hardening.py, and leave test_locale_de.py and test_locale_overrides.py alone because they use the setters for real.",
          "effort": "small",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::test_strategy::duplicated_locale_reset_fixture"
          ],
          "done": true
        }
      ]
    },
    "dead-code-and-residue-deletion": {
      "name": "dead-code-and-residue-deletion",
      "description": "Delete provably unreachable code inside src/weewx_ha: the two unit_system None guards in config_publisher.py and state_publisher.py, the three RuntimeError cache guards in utils.py, the redundant MQTT credential guard in controller.py, and the duplicated function-level import in config_publisher.py.",
      "issue_ids": [
        "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::always_true_unit_system_checks",
        "review::.::holistic::type_safety::dead_none_guard_unit_system",
        "review::.::holistic::ai_generated_debt::unreachable_none_guards",
        "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::redundant_none_guards_and_lazy_caches",
        "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::redundant_credential_guard",
        "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::stale_local_import_config_publisher"
      ],
