      "auto": false,
      "cluster_key": "",
      "action": null,
      "action_type": "manual_fix",
      "execution_policy": "planned_only",
      "execution_status": "done",
      "user_modified": true,
      "priority": 6,
      "depends_on_clusters": [
        "locale-cache-invalidation",
        "controller-callback-typing-and-submit"
      ],
      "action_steps": [
        {
          "title": "Delete the two dead unit_system None guards",
          "detail": "Unwrap `if self.unit_system is not None:` at src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py:119 and src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py:67 down to a plain `packet = to_std_system(packet, int(self.unit_system))`. The verdict is DELETE, not harden, on five verified proofs: ExtensionConfig.unit_system (src/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py:48-50) is a non-Optional UnitSystem with a METRICWX default; pydantic rejects None for it outright; both publisher constructors declare the same non-Optional default (src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py:48, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py:39); the only two call sites pass self.config.unit_system (src/weewx_ha/controller.py:144 and :151); and `pipenv run pytest --cov=weewx_ha --cov-report=term-missing` reports the partial branches `119->121` for config_publisher.py and `67->69` for state_publisher.py, i.e. the None arm of each is never taken. Any executor proposal to harden these paths against None must be REFUSED with this evidence -- this cluster settles the plan's one genuine contradiction.",
          "effort": "trivial",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::always_true_unit_system_checks",
            "review::.::holistic::type_safety::dead_none_guard_unit_system",
            "review::.::holistic::ai_generated_debt::unreachable_none_guards",
            "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::redundant_none_guards_and_lazy_caches"
          ],
          "done": true
        },
        {
          "title": "Delete the redundant credential guard and the duplicated local import",
          "detail": "Two deletions. (a) `if mqtt_config.username and mqtt_config.password` at src/weewx_ha/controller.py:178 can never be False: username is `str = Field(..., min_length=1)` (src/weewx_ha/models/mqtt_config.py:29-31), password is a required `Secret[str]` with a non-empty validator (:22-24 and :36-41), and bool(Secret('')) was measured to be True anyway. Call client.username_pw_set at :179-181 unconditionally and strip the security framing from the finding: there is no anonymous-connect path to create. (b) CORRECTION to the organize text -- the function-level `from .utils import get_key_config_dict` at src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py:160 has NO module-level twin. The import at :14 is `from .utils import UnitSystem, get_key_config, get_unit_metadata` and does not include get_key_config_dict, so deleting :160 on its own leaves a NameError at :166; add get_key_config_dict to the :14 import in the same edit. Verified safe: there is no cycle on that edge, since src/weewx_ha/utils.py imports only .locale_loader, and src/weewx_ha/__init__.py:12 already imports utils before config_publisher at :14.",
          "effort": "trivial",
          "issue_refs": [
            "review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::redundant_credential_guard",
            "review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::stale_local_import_config_publisher"
          ],
          "done": true
        }
      ]
    },
