    {
      "timestamp": "2026-11-10T11:39:21+00:00",
      "action": "triage_confirm_reflect",
      "issue_ids": [],
      "cluster_name": null,
      "actor": "user",
      "note": null,
      "detail": {
        "attestation": "I reviewed the reflect stage against the persisted ledger: 66 cited IDs, no missing and no duplicate entries, and 66 ledger rows splitting 44 cluster / 22 permanent_skip, which matches the reported 44 in PR #1, 16 deferred to the follow-up PR and 6 genuinely skipped. The split honours the rule I set for this cycle -- behaviour-correcting fixes and local cleanups in already-touched files stay in the bugfix PR, every structural refactor (import topology, module decomposition, api naming) is deferred with its destination named so the follow-up PR can be opened from plan state. The four reproduced defects in logic_clarity, contract_coherence and initialization_coupling lead the order, and the settled questions (dead unit_system guards deleted, to_std_system safe, get_key_config claim rejected, time_zone field kept) are carried as decisions rather than left open. One reservation I will act on at organize: the locale-loader-error-contract cluster turns a tolerated missing packaged YAML into a hard startup failure, which is a risk change rather than a defect fix, so it does not belong in this PR on the rule as written."
      }
    },
