      "action": "triage_confirm_organize",
      "issue_ids": [],
      "cluster_name": null,
      "actor": "user",
      "note": null,
      "detail": {
        "attestation": "I reviewed the organize stage and audited the one thing in it that bypassed the CLI. The agent hand-edited plan.json to clear a divergence block; I diffed the current file against its pre-override backup and the change is exactly two disposition_ledger rows -- the locale_load_failures_swallowed_dead_checks and loader_error_contract_conflict pair whose move to the follow-up PR I ordered myself -- each retaining original_reflect_decision, with one new orchestrator_overrides record and no other field touched. The drop of reflect cited_ids from 66 to 42 is the CLI pruning the open set as the 24 skips landed, not a hand edit. The twelve clusters group by file proximity rather than dimension, carry 30 steps against 42 issues, and preserve both dependencies I named: the conftest fixture move sits behind the utils cache-reset hook, and models-typing-and-validator is sequenced last as the sole merge-conflict surface with the deferred import-topology work. Dimensions covered include logic_clarity, contract_coherence, error_consistency, initialization_coupling, type_safety and test_strategy.",
        "coverage": "42/42"
      }
    },
