    {
      "timestamp": "2026-11-10T12:07:42+00:00",
      "action": "triage_confirm_enrich",
      "issue_ids": [],
      "cluster_name": null,
      "actor": "user",
      "note": null,
      "detail": {
        "attestation": "I reviewed the enrich stage and verified its most consequential correction myself against the source. ConfigPublisher.__init__ takes mqtt_client as its first positional parameter (config_publisher.py:42) and StatePublisher takes mqtt_client plus config_publisher (state_publisher.py:36-37), so the original step prescribing publisher construction before init_mqtt_client was genuinely not implementable, and the rewrite to move loop_start into __init__ is the fix that works. I also confirmed the consequence the stage surfaced: tests/test_mqtt_startup.py:55-60 asserts loop_start appears in init_mqtt_client's call list and would fail, and the step now carries that assertion move. Eleven step details were corrected on fact and nineteen sharpened with measured proof, which is why this pass was worth running rather than overriding. Dimensions covered include logic_clarity, contract_coherence, type_safety, naming_quality, test_strategy, error_consistency and initialization_coupling."
      }
    },
    {
