    },
    {
      "timestamp": "2026-11-10T12:15:11+00:00",
      "action": "triage_confirm_sense_check",
      "issue_ids": [],
      "cluster_name": null,
      "actor": "user",
      "note": null,
      "detail": {
        "attestation": "I merged three independent sense-check passes (content, structure, value) and recorded the stage myself so they would not write to plan.json concurrently. I re-verified the two findings that reverse earlier stages before accepting them: removing the three RuntimeError guards from utils.py adds three mypy return-value errors against a baseline of one, so they are type-narrowing rather than dead code and dead-code-and-residue-deletion step 2 is dropped; and the _LAMBDA_REGISTRY names are user-facing convert_lambda vocabulary reachable through the sensors override option, so timestamp-lambda-naming is a silent breaking change and is deferred. The ledger covers all twelve clusters exactly once: preprocessor-battery-bitmap keep; controller-init-lifecycle-contract, locale-cache-invalidation, dead-code-and-residue-deletion, coverage-gaps-controller-and-catalogue and dependency-and-readme-hygiene tighten; archive-derived-atomic-update, controller-callback-typing-and-submit, timestamp-lambda-naming, mypy-weewx-import-overrides, models-typing-and-validator and docstring-and-entry-log-trim skipped to the follow-up PR. PR #1 drops from 30 steps to 12."
      }
    },
