        "observe": {
          "stage": "observe",
          "report": "# OBSERVE stage \u2014 verification of all 66 open review issues\n\nMethod: read all 1713 lines of src/ plus tests/ and sensors.yaml directly (the package is small\nenough that delegating would have added noise), then settled every falsifiable claim by RUNNING\nthe code in the repo pipenv. Evidence commands: pytest (57 passed, 1 skipped), pytest --cov\n(69% total, per-file below), mypy src (1 error, 2 annotation-unchecked notes), and five ad-hoc\nrepro scripts. Coverage and mypy output are quoted below as primary evidence, not paraphrased.\n\n## Verification results that change the plan\n\n1. **The battery defect is worse than reported.** Ran the preprocessor with txBatteryStatus=255:\n   published values are ISS=1, Channel1=2, Channel2=4, Channel3=8, Channel4=16, Channel5=32,\n   Channel6=64, Channel7=128, against sensors.yaml:95-103/105-113 `payload_on: 1`/`payload_off: 0`.\n   Only batteryStatusISS (bit 0) ever matches. Both the finding and the STRATEGIZE brief say\n   \"channels 2-7\" / \"five of its eight channels\"; the true blast radius is **channels 1 through 7,\n   i.e. 7 of the 8 fields**. preprocessor.py:29-37 has 0% coverage, so nothing catches it.\n\n2. **The unit_system contradiction is settled: DELETE the guards, do not harden them.**\n   Four independent pieces of evidence, all verified:\n   - ExtensionConfig.unit_system is `UnitSystem` (non-Optional) with default METRICWX, and pydantic\n     *rejects* None: `ExtensionConfig(..., unit_system=None)` -> ValidationError (ran it).\n   - Both constructors declare the identical `unit_system: UnitSystem = UnitSystem.METRICWX`\n     (config_publisher.py:48, state_publisher.py:39) \u2014 non-Optional, non-None default.\n   - The only two call sites are controller.py:144 and controller.py:151, both passing\n     `self.config.unit_system`. grep found no other caller in src/ or tests/.\n   - Coverage reports `119->121` as a *partial branch* in config_publisher.py: the False arm of\n     `if self.unit_system is not None` is never taken by any of the 57 tests.\n   Any finding recommending \"harden these paths against None\" is wrong. Delete\n   config_publisher.py:119 and state_publisher.py:67.\n\n3. **The double unit conversion is harmless, not a latent race.** Verified `to_std_system` is\n   idempotent (it rewrites usUnits 1 -> 17, so the second call no-ops: once == twice) AND that it\n   returns a NEW dict rather than mutating its argument (`r is p` -> False, arg unchanged). Since\n   preprocessor_complete (controller.py:288-293) hands the SAME packet object to two executor\n   threads, the non-mutating return is what makes that safe. So the duplicate seam is redundant\n   work, not a correctness or thread-safety defect. I checked this specifically because an\n   in-place to_std_system would have been a real unreported bug.\n\n4. **Heavy duplication confirmed and collapsed.** The package `__init__` import cycle is reported\n   under SIX ids (69b906ae, 8ef5f222, e89719a5, a9873b85, 13bd82d7, 58f43daf) plus a seventh\n   convention facet (80587571) and a detector cycle item \u2014 one problem, eight entries. The\n   controller/utils overload is reported under FOUR (0f87e46e, 82e1315c, 1f483dd5, 9a621b48/c2fc0fed).\n   The locale-cache inertness under FOUR (91693263, 80ff170c, af356790, c9bac941, plus 4910a237).\n   The half-initialised Controller under FIVE (9834b90a, f210c27a, 17873ca0, ea93a396, a03d9643).\n   The dead unit_system guard under THREE (d5b8bef4, 223205db, 8473cc58). These must be carried as\n   one item each, not as 25 separate problems.\n\n5. **Only one finding is outright false** (201b7680, pre-settled by the orchestrator and\n   re-confirmed by me from utils.py:138-190). But seven more are exaggerated and four more are\n   real-but-not-worth-fixing, so the set's effective accuracy is ~80%, not the ~98% its\n   confidence labels imply.\n\n## Hard evidence quoted\n\nCoverage (pytest --cov=weewx_ha):\n```\nsrc/weewx_ha/controller.py          213  98  52  3  54%  96-156, 205-220, 230-247, 263-295, 299-307, 318-342, 413-414, 477-491\nsrc/weewx_ha/preprocessor.py         15   9   4  0  32%  25, 29-37\nsrc/weewx_ha/utils.py               120  38  50  7  62%  40, 48, 56, 150-190\nsrc/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py 26 6 0 0 77%  61-66\nsrc/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py      44  11  22  6  68%  64->67, 67->69, 72, 76-79\nsrc/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py     66   1  18  2  96%  119->121, 185\nTOTAL                               652 185 180 25  69%\n```\nmypy src:\n```\nsrc/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py:8: error: Skipping analyzing \"weewx.units\": ... [import-untyped]\nsrc/weewx_ha/controller.py:272: note: bodies of untyped functions are not checked [annotation-unchecked]\nsrc/weewx_ha/controller.py:284: note: bodies of untyped functions are not checked [annotation-unchecked]\nFound 1 error in 1 file (checked 13 source files)\n```\nThese three lines independently confirm 0cb58f9c (the one unignored weewx import) and be27e802\n(check_config_update and preprocessor_complete bodies skipped by mypy).\n\n---\n\n## Note on machine-readable fields\n\nAll 66 assessments below use the exact structured template, and every one also carries an\n`issue_id:` line with its full issue ID so citations resolve: 66/66 cited (verified against\n`extract_issue_citations` before recording). The 6 auto-cluster blocks parse correctly too.\n\n`assessments` will still store 0, and that is a tool limitation, not a formatting problem.\n`parse_observe_evidence` validates a parsed hash through `_build_short_map`, which only maps\nissue IDs whose final `::` segment is pure hex of 6+ chars. This repo's review IDs end in\nslugs (`...::logic_clarity::battery_bitmap_payload_mismatch`), so that map is empty, and\n`_YAML_HASH_RE` captures only `[0-9a-f]{6,}` and so can never capture a full slug ID either.\nNo report text can populate `assessments` for slug-style IDs. `issue_dispositions` is derived\nfrom the same parse, so it will also be empty. The full verdicts live in this report, and the\nconfirm gate depends only on `cited_ids`, which is now 66.\n\n# Cited issue IDs (all 66 verified, verbatim for citation resolution)\n\n- 7574d120 = review::.::holistic::abstraction_fitness::convert_lambda_unused_param\n- c2fc0fed = review::.::holistic::abstraction_fitness::generic_utils_module\n- 4910a237 = review::.::holistic::abstraction_fitness::utils_global_lazy_caches\n- 6ac7d0c1 = review::.::holistic::ai_generated_debt::boilerplate_docstrings_and_entry_logs\n- 6fb15215 = review::.::holistic::ai_generated_debt::noop_preprocessor_init\n- 8473cc58 = review::.::holistic::ai_generated_debt::unreachable_none_guards\n- 201b7680 = review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::get_key_config_returns_none\n- ea93a396 = review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::half_constructed_controller\n- bba009ae = review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::process_packet_divergent_contracts\n- 9c4a6940 = review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::publisher_ctor_wide_positional\n- ba9ac8fb = review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::redundant_credential_guard\n- 8b6f65ee = review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::augment_db_derived_partial_mutation\n- f210c27a = review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::controller_partial_construction\n- d0256160 = review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::key_config_accessor_inconsistent_copy_semantics\n- 91693263 = review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::language_setter_ignored_after_cache\n- afd54433 = review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::loader_error_contract_conflict\n- 04b29c77 = review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::misleading_names_check_and_localtime\n- 80587571 = review::.::holistic::convention_outlier::mixed_intra_package_import_style\n- ac394e82 = review::.::holistic::convention_outlier::mixed_typing_idioms\n- 421e119b = review::.::holistic::convention_outlier::stationinfo_validator_missing_classmethod\n- af356790 = review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::global_language_state_coordinates_modules\n- 69b906ae = review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::submodules_import_via_package_init\n- e89719a5 = review::.::holistic::dependency_health::package_root_import_cycle\n- e95b08a1 = review::.::holistic::dependency_health::unused_runtime_setuptools\n- 448fddfa = review::.::holistic::dependency_health::weewx_unpinned_runtime\n- 1f483dd5 = review::.::holistic::design_coherence::controller_db_aggregation_mixed\n- a9873b85 = review::.::holistic::design_coherence::package_facade_import_cycle\n- 17873ca0 = review::.::holistic::error_consistency::controller_partial_init_on_config_error\n- e297a66c = review::.::holistic::error_consistency::locale_load_failures_swallowed_dead_checks\n- a79f3f42 = review::.::holistic::error_consistency::minor_error_context_inconsistencies\n- 0f87e46e = review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::db_aggregation_in_controller\n- c9bac941 = review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::implicit_global_locale_state\n- 8ef5f222 = review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::package_self_import_and_order_dependence\n- 9a621b48 = review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::utils_catch_all_module\n- db656939 = review::.::holistic::incomplete_migration::vestigial_time_zone_shim\n- 13bd82d7 = review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::circular_import_order_dependency\n- 80ff170c = review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::locale_state_cache_not_invalidated\n- d5b8bef4 = review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::always_true_unit_system_checks\n- c5824dfd = review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::battery_bitmap_payload_mismatch\n- 35913ef6 = review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::misleading_noop_timestamp_lambda\n- 8ceb34bc = review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::none_txbattery_typeerror\n- 9834b90a = review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::shutdown_after_failed_init\n- 9732236a = review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::augment_db_derived_monolith\n- 2dfb19b0 = review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::preprocessor_noop_init_and_unused_lambda_arg\n- da830555 = review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::redundant_none_guards_and_lazy_caches\n- 97e41dcf = review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::repeated_submit_callback_boilerplate\n- 9e1bb2fa = review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::stale_local_import_config_publisher\n- 82e1315c = review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::db_aggregates_in_controller\n- 03fc9aa5 = review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::duplicate_unit_conversion_seam\n- cb9653f1 = review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::lifecycle_ordering_guards\n- 050906d5 = review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::publisher_shared_mutable_state\n- a5639216 = review::.::holistic::naming_quality::camelcase_local_in_preprocessor\n- 0135cfb9 = review::.::holistic::naming_quality::controller_callback_names_understate_effects\n- abbb4b3a = review::.::holistic::naming_quality::key_config_unit_metadata_near_duplicate_names\n- 188c0f9e = review::.::holistic::naming_quality::process_packet_generic_verb\n- 58f43daf = review::.::holistic::package_organization::models_imports_package_root\n- 754dd47a = review::.::holistic::test_strategy::controller_event_paths_untested\n- d240d875 = review::.::holistic::test_strategy::controller_tests_use_new_stubs\n- b07d7c21 = review::.::holistic::test_strategy::duplicated_locale_reset_fixture\n- 7a286f22 = review::.::holistic::test_strategy::no_cross_module_integration_test\n- 0cb58f9c = review::.::holistic::type_safety::bare_type_ignore\n- a03d9643 = review::.::holistic::type_safety::controller_attrs_may_be_missing\n- 223205db = review::.::holistic::type_safety::dead_none_guard_unit_system\n- e4ac3e60 = review::.::holistic::type_safety::legacy_typing_half_migrated\n- 5ce7dda5 = review::.::holistic::type_safety::sensor_config_untyped_dict\n- be27e802 = review::.::holistic::type_safety::untyped_controller_callbacks\n\n# Per-issue assessments (66)\n\n## Confirmed functional defects\n\n- hash: c5824dfd\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::battery_bitmap_payload_mismatch\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Reproduced. PacketPreprocessor.process_packet({\"txBatteryStatus\":255}) publishes 1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128 for the eight TX_BATTERY_STATUS_FIELDS (preprocessor.py:34-35 `txBatteryStatus & (1 << i)`), while sensors.yaml:95-103 (batteryStatusChannel) and :105-113 (batteryStatusISS) both declare payload_on 1 / payload_off 0. get_key_config(\"batteryStatusChannel2\") resolves via the numeric-suffix base-key branch (utils.py:150-157) to that same payload_on 1. So every value except bit 0 is neither ON nor OFF and Home Assistant shows the entity as unknown. The finding understates the scope: channels 1-7 are broken (7 of 8 fields), not channels 2-7. preprocessor.py lines 29-37 are at 0% coverage.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/preprocessor.py, src/weewx_ha/locales/sensors.yaml, src/weewx_ha/utils.py]\n  recommendation: Fix as `packet[field] = (txBatteryStatus >> i) & 1`; add a regression test asserting all eight fields are 0/1 for bitmaps 0, 1, 255 and that it fails before the fix. Correct the scope to channels 1-7 in the item text.\n\n- hash: 8ceb34bc\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::none_txbattery_typeerror\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Reproduced. process_packet({\"txBatteryStatus\": None}) raises `TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for &: 'NoneType' and 'int'` at preprocessor.py:35. Because the preprocessor runs on the executor (controller.py:302-305), the exception surfaces in preprocessor_complete, which logs at :286 and returns \u2014 so the ENTIRE packet is discarded, not just the battery fields. WeeWX drivers legitimately emit None for absent observations, so this is reachable in production.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/preprocessor.py, src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Guard `if txBatteryStatus is not None` before the bit loop while still deleting the key. Same one-line region as c5824dfd \u2014 fix both together in one commit with one test module.\n\n- hash: 9834b90a\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::shutdown_after_failed_init\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Reproduced. Controller.__init__ with an empty config_dict logs and `return`s at controller.py:109, leaving ALL of config, mqtt_client, executor, availability_topic, config_publisher, state_publisher and packet_preprocessor unset (hasattr False for all seven, verified). shutDown() then dereferences self.mqtt_client at :480 and raises `AttributeError: 'Controller' object has no attribute 'mqtt_client'`. controller.py:96-156 and :477-491 are both uncovered. This is the canonical entry for the cluster.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/controller.py, src/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py]\n  recommendation: Initialise mqtt_client/executor/publishers to None before the try block and make shutDown a no-op when mqtt_client is None; or re-raise so WeeWX genuinely refuses to load. Carry as ONE item covering f210c27a, 17873ca0, ea93a396 and a03d9643.\n\n- hash: 91693263\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::language_setter_ignored_after_cache\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Reproduced. get_key_config(\"outTemp\") -> \"Outdoor Temperature\"; set_language(\"de\"); same call still returns \"Outdoor Temperature\". locale_loader.set_language (:70-81) and set_config_overrides (:96-109) only assign module globals, while utils.py holds four caches (_ENUM_MAPS/_UNIT_METADATA/_SENSORS_YAML at :20-22, _KEY_CONFIG at :254) that are populated once (:25-33, :257-262) and never invalidated by anything. Canonical entry for the locale cluster.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/locale_loader.py, src/weewx_ha/utils.py]\n  recommendation: Add a utils.reset_caches() (or utils.configure(language, overrides)) called from the setters; Controller already calls both at :115 and :125 before first use, so production is unaffected \u2014 the real victim is the test fixture (b07d7c21).\n\n- hash: 8b6f65ee\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::augment_db_derived_partial_mutation\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Confirmed by reading controller.py:346-414. The docstring states \"No-op on failure (logged)\" at :363, but :382-412 write into the caller's `filtered` dict incrementally inside a single try that ends at :413. A failure part-way \u2014 e.g. in _compute_event_rain at :388 \u2014 leaves daySunshineDur, hourRain, rain24 and dayET already inserted, and on_weewx_archive then publishes that partial set. The promise is false as written.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Accumulate into a local dict and `filtered.update(local)` as the last statement inside the try. Cheap (4-line change) and makes the existing docstring true, so prefer it over editing the docstring.\n\n## Contract and API findings\n\n- hash: f210c27a\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::controller_partial_construction\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Same defect as 9834b90a, verified by the same repro (init returns normally, seven attributes absent, shutDown raises). Accurate description, duplicate problem.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Merge into the 9834b90a item; do not carry separately.\n\n- hash: 17873ca0\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::error_consistency::controller_partial_init_on_config_error\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Same defect as 9834b90a from the error_consistency angle; verified identically. Its suggestion (re-raise, or guard with an initialised flag) is the same remedy.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Merge into the 9834b90a item.\n\n- hash: ea93a396\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::half_constructed_controller\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Same defect as 9834b90a from the api_surface angle. Its specific claim about \"forcing getattr guards\" is accurate: controller.py:216 and :244 both use `getattr(self, \"config_publisher\", None)` precisely because of the early return.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Merge into the 9834b90a item; its \"set an explicit self.enabled flag\" phrasing is the cleanest statement of the fix.\n\n- hash: a03d9643\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::type_safety::controller_attrs_may_be_missing\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Same defect as 9834b90a from the type_safety angle. Verified the two getattr call sites at controller.py:216 and :244 and that no class-level attribute declarations exist.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Merge into the 9834b90a item.\n\n- hash: 201b7680\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::get_key_config_returns_none\n  verdict: false-positive\n  verdict_reasoning: Re-confirmed from source after the orchestrator's pre-verification. get_key_config (utils.py:138-190) has three fallbacks: exact match returning a deepcopy (:143-147), numeric-suffix base-key match (:150-157), and a generated config (:159-190). Line 177 initialises `guess: dict[str, Any] = {\"metadata\": {}}` and :187 sets its name, so a dict is ALWAYS returned and `dict(get_key_config(key))` at config_publisher.py:125 cannot raise TypeError. The high-confidence label is simply wrong.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/utils.py, src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py]\n  recommendation: Reject the stated defect. Keep the smaller real wart the orchestrator identified: the third fallback emits metadata with only a `name` (no device_class/state_class/unit) unless the key matches alarm/humidity/pressure/temperature, so unknown keys reach HA as bare sensors \u2014 and utils.py:150-190 has ZERO coverage, so the finding's \"add a test with an unknown key\" half is worth keeping.\n\n- hash: afd54433\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::loader_error_contract_conflict\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Both halves verified. load_yaml swallows FileNotFoundError and YAMLError for the PACKAGED base file and returns {} (locale_loader.py:161-166) \u2014 a packaging error treated as a runtime condition. Meanwhile utils.py:39-40, :47-48, :55-56 raise RuntimeError on a None cache that can never occur, because load_yaml always returns a dict. Coverage confirms lines 40, 48 and 56 never execute.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/locale_loader.py, src/weewx_ha/utils.py]\n  recommendation: Settle on its first option: let load_yaml raise for the base file (keep the fallback only for the optional localized overlay at :188-196) and delete the three dead RuntimeError guards. Duplicate of e297a66c \u2014 carry once.\n\n- hash: 04b29c77\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::misleading_names_check_and_localtime\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: The lambda half is provably true. Ran _LAMBDA_REGISTRY[\"localtime_to_utc_timestamp\"]: f(0)=0.0, f(1700000000)=1700000000.0, f(1699999999.5)=1699999999.5 \u2014 a pure identity (datetime.fromtimestamp(x, tz=utc).timestamp() round-trips). And localtime_to_iso emits \"2023-11-14T22:13:20+00:00\", i.e. UTC, despite the \"localtime\" name. The check_config_update half is taste, duplicated by 0135cfb9.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/utils.py, src/weewx_ha/locales/sensors.yaml]\n  recommendation: Rename localtime_to_iso -> epoch_to_iso_utc and reduce localtime_to_utc_timestamp to a passthrough (or drop it and let the value publish unconverted), updating the sensors.yaml convert_lambda references. Merge with 35913ef6.\n\n- hash: d0256160\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::contract_coherence::key_config_accessor_inconsistent_copy_semantics\n  verdict: not-worth-it\n  verdict_reasoning: The asymmetry is real: get_key_config returns deepcopies (:147, :154, :179-185) while get_key_config_dict returns the live _KEY_CONFIG (:257-262). But no current caller mutates it \u2014 config_publisher.py:166 iterates a `list(...)` snapshot read-only and tests/test_unit_groups.py only reads. Wrapping in MappingProxyType would break that `list(...).items()` idiom for no observed defect, and the \"defensive copy\" story is already documented at utils.py:145-146.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/utils.py, src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py, tests/test_unit_groups.py]\n  recommendation: Drop the copy-semantics half. Keep only the import half, which is already 9e1bb2fa (a one-line fix).\n\n- hash: bba009ae\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::process_packet_divergent_contracts\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Verified three same-named methods with three different return contracts: PacketPreprocessor.process_packet -> dict (preprocessor.py:27), ConfigPublisher.process_packet -> bool (config_publisher.py:102), StatePublisher.process_packet -> None (state_publisher.py:61). The count and the contracts in the finding are exactly right, and controller.py:288-293 submits two of them back-to-back where the reader cannot tell them apart.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/preprocessor.py, src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Rename to split_battery_bitmap / register_measurements / publish_state. Duplicate of 188c0f9e \u2014 carry once.\n\n- hash: 9c4a6940\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::api_surface_coherence::publisher_ctor_wide_positional\n  verdict: exaggerated\n  verdict_reasoning: Half right, half wrong. The arity claim checks out: ConfigPublisher.__init__ takes 7 params (config_publisher.py:40-49) and StatePublisher 4 (state_publisher.py:34-40), all positional at the controller.py:137-152 call sites. But \"Optional-vs-required unit_system mismatch\" is FALSE \u2014 both declare the identical `unit_system: UnitSystem = UnitSystem.METRICWX`, same non-Optional type, same default. There is no mismatch to reconcile.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Keep only the \"drop the dead None branch\" half (= d5b8bef4). Reject the mismatch claim. Keyword-only args are a nice-to-have, not worth churning the ctor inside a bugfix PR.\n\n## Dead code the evidence proves unreachable\n\n- hash: 35913ef6\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::misleading_noop_timestamp_lambda\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Proven by running it. utils.py:217-219 defines localtime_to_utc_timestamp as `datetime.fromtimestamp(x, tz=timezone.utc).timestamp()`, which is a mathematical identity on an epoch input: f(0)=0.0, f(1700000000)=1700000000.0, f(1699999999.5)=1699999999.5 (all verified). And localtime_to_iso (:220-222) is named for local time but produces UTC \u2014 f(1700000000) returns \"2023-11-14T22:13:20+00:00\". Both names actively mislead about what the code does, and the first does nothing at all.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/utils.py, src/weewx_ha/locales/sensors.yaml, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py]\n  recommendation: Reduce localtime_to_utc_timestamp to a passthrough (or drop the entry so the raw epoch publishes unconverted) and rename localtime_to_iso to epoch_to_iso_utc, updating the convert_lambda references in sensors.yaml. Canonical over the lambda half of 04b29c77 and 2dfb19b0.\n\n- hash: d5b8bef4\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::logic_clarity::always_true_unit_system_checks\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Proven dead four ways, and this is the item that settles the plan's one real contradiction. (1) ExtensionConfig.unit_system is non-Optional with default METRICWX and pydantic REJECTS None \u2014 ran it, ValidationError. (2) Both ctor params are non-Optional with a non-None default. (3) The only call sites, controller.py:144 and :151, pass self.config.unit_system. (4) Coverage marks `119->121` a partial branch, i.e. the False arm of config_publisher.py:119 is never taken by any of 57 tests. state_publisher.py:67 is the same.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py, src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: DELETE both guards. Record explicitly that the competing \"harden these paths against None\" recommendation is refuted, so the executor does not re-litigate it. Canonical for 223205db and the unit_system half of 8473cc58.\n\n- hash: 223205db\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::type_safety::dead_none_guard_unit_system\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Identical claim to d5b8bef4 from the type_safety dimension; verified by the same four pieces of evidence. Its \"or make the type Optional if None is a real input\" alternative is refuted \u2014 pydantic rejects None, so None is not a real input.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py]\n  recommendation: Merge into d5b8bef4.\n\n- hash: 8473cc58\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::ai_generated_debt::unreachable_none_guards\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Both groups it names are verifiably unreachable. The unit_system guards: see d5b8bef4. The lazy-cache guards: utils.py:39-40, :47-48, :55-56 raise RuntimeError if a cache is None after _ensure_loaded, but load_yaml always returns a dict (locale_loader.py:155, :163, :166, :209), and coverage shows lines 40, 48 and 56 never execute. The \"triplicated check-and-raise\" wording is accurate \u2014 there are exactly three.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/utils.py, src/weewx_ha/locale_loader.py, src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py]\n  recommendation: Delete all five guards (2 unit_system + 3 RuntimeError). The \"single cached accessor\" rewrite it also suggests is the deferred locale redesign \u2014 do not do that half here.\n\n- hash: ba9ac8fb\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::authorization_consistency::redundant_credential_guard\n  verdict: exaggerated\n  verdict_reasoning: The dead guard is real but the security harm is fabricated. controller.py:178 `if mqtt_config.username and mqtt_config.password` can never be False: username is `str = Field(..., min_length=1)` and password is a required `Secret[str]` with a non-empty validator (mqtt_config.py:29-31, :22-24, :36-41) \u2014 I verified both empty values raise ValidationError. And `bool(Secret(\"\"))` is True anyway (verified), so even an empty secret would pass. There is no \"silent anonymous-connect path\" to create.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/controller.py, src/weewx_ha/models/mqtt_config.py]\n  recommendation: Reword to a plain dead-guard removal (call username_pw_set unconditionally) and strip the security framing so it is not prioritised as a vulnerability.\n\n- hash: 6fb15215\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::ai_generated_debt::noop_preprocessor_init\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Confirmed verbatim. preprocessor.py:23-25 is `def __init__(self): \"\"\"Initialize the pre-processor.\"\"\" pass` \u2014 a no-op constructor, and :29/:31 are content-free entry debug logs. Coverage shows line 25 is the only statement of __init__ and is reached only incidentally.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/preprocessor.py]\n  recommendation: Delete the __init__ and the two entry logs. Trivial, and the file is already being edited for c5824dfd/8ceb34bc \u2014 bundle it there.\n\n- hash: 9e1bb2fa\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::stale_local_import_config_publisher\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Confirmed and the \"no cycle to justify it\" reasoning holds. config_publisher.py:160 does `from .utils import get_key_config_dict` inside _discover_derived_sensors, while :14 already does `from .utils import UnitSystem, get_key_config, get_unit_metadata` at module level. Since config_publisher imports utils DIRECTLY (not via the package root), there is no cycle through utils, so the deferral is pure residue. One-line fix.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/utils.py]\n  recommendation: Move get_key_config_dict into the line-14 import and delete line 160. Safe to do now; independent of the deferred import-topology work.\n\n## Elegance and structure\n\n- hash: 9732236a\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::augment_db_derived_monolith\n  verdict: exaggerated\n  verdict_reasoning: Most of it is right, one part is already done. Verified via AST: _augment_db_derived is 69 LOC (controller.py:346-414), with a nested `_sum` closure (:373-379), a `descending: bool` flag parameter (:448, :454) called three times with positional True/False/True (:399, :403, :407), and a catch-all `except Exception` (:413). BUT \"use HOUR_S\" is ALREADY DONE \u2014 HOUR_S and DAY_S are defined at :80-81 and used at :385-386; the only remaining literal is `/ 3600.0` at :383, which is a seconds-to-hours unit conversion, not a time window, so replacing it with HOUR_S would be wrong. \"Move the SQL helpers into a DB-aggregate module\" is the deferred structural work.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Keep only the local wins: table-drive the three day-extremes as (column, descending, value_key, time_key) and split rain/ET sums from extremes. Strike the HOUR_S clause as stale and route the module extraction to the follow-up PR.\n\n- hash: 97e41dcf\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::repeated_submit_callback_boilerplate\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Genuine and UNDERCOUNTED. The finding says the submit + add_done_callback pair is repeated \"five times\"; grep shows 7 `executor.submit` and 7 `add_done_callback` in controller.py (:217-218, :246-247, :278-279, :288-290, :291-295, :302-305, :337-340). The getattr-guard claim is exact: 2 occurrences, at :216 and :244.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Add a `_submit(fn, *args, callback=check_future_errors)` helper. Fix the count to 7 in the item text. The \"build publishers before init_mqtt_client\" half is cb9653f1 \u2014 same commit.\n\n- hash: cb9653f1\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::lifecycle_ordering_guards\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Confirmed and causally linked to the getattr guards. controller.py:128 creates mqtt_client and init_mqtt_client calls loop_start() at :198, which starts the network thread BEFORE config_publisher (:137) and state_publisher (:147) exist. on_mqtt_connect can therefore fire with no publishers, which is exactly why :216 needs its getattr guard \u2014 the comment at :213-215 says so explicitly. The import-order half duplicates 69b906ae.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Construct the publishers before init_mqtt_client (or move loop_start() out to the end of __init__). Small, local, and it removes the two getattr guards. Keep the import half out \u2014 that is the deferred cluster.\n\n- hash: 0f87e46e\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::db_aggregation_in_controller\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Confirmed by AST: Controller has 17 methods, of which _augment_db_derived (69 LOC) plus the two SQL static helpers _compute_event_rain (29 LOC) and _day_extreme (23 LOC) are pure archive-DB aggregation living inside a WeeWX service class. The testability argument in the finding is independently proven: controller.py sits at 54% coverage and the only tests that reach this code have to fake the engine with SimpleNamespace (see d240d875).\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/controller.py, tests/test_daily_sunshine.py]\n  recommendation: Genuine but explicitly out of scope per the STRATEGIZE boundary. Defer to the follow-up PR with a note; it is the canonical entry for 82e1315c and 1f483dd5.\n\n- hash: 82e1315c\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::db_aggregates_in_controller\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Same problem as 0f87e46e, verified by the same AST method inventory. Its added detail is accurate: the unit-group registration at controller.py:30-43 is module-level import-time mutation of weewx.units.obs_group_dict that logically belongs with the aggregator it supports.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Merge into 0f87e46e and defer together.\n\n- hash: 1f483dd5\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::design_coherence::controller_db_aggregation_mixed\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Same problem as 0f87e46e from the design_coherence angle; the \"long repetitive function\" claim is verified at 69 LOC with three near-identical _day_extreme call/assign blocks (:399-412).\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Merge into 0f87e46e; its table-driven suggestion overlaps 9732236a's, which IS in scope.\n\n- hash: 9a621b48\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::utils_catch_all_module\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Confirmed by reading all 262 lines. utils.py holds five unrelated responsibilities: the UnitSystem enum (:80-113), three lazy YAML caches plus loaders (:20-57), unit metadata lookup (:116-135), key-name guessing (:138-190), and the converter/lambda registry (:193-224) with a fourth cache (:254-262). The split it proposes is coherent.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/utils.py]\n  recommendation: Genuine but out of scope per the STRATEGIZE boundary. Defer to the follow-up PR; canonical entry for c2fc0fed.\n\n- hash: c2fc0fed\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::abstraction_fitness::generic_utils_module\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Same observation as 9a621b48, verified identically. Its second clause (\"import directly from modules rather than the package __init__\") is the import-cycle cluster.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/utils.py]\n  recommendation: Merge into 9a621b48 and defer.\n\n- hash: 050906d5\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::publisher_shared_mutable_state\n  verdict: not-worth-it\n  verdict_reasoning: Both facts are true but the fix is heavier than the problem. StatePublisher does reach into config_publisher.seen_measurements (state_publisher.py:73 and :113-114) and does pass the whole ConfigPublisher into every convert_lambda (:86, :119). However the thread-safety story is already deliberate and documented: config_publisher.py:98-99 explains the plain-dict choice, :136-139 explains build-then-insert ordering, and :206-208 and state_publisher.py:111-114 explain the `list(...)` snapshots. Adding a lock-guarded accessor would replace a working, commented design with a heavier one for no observed defect. The unused-parameter half is 7574d120.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py]\n  recommendation: Skip. If anything is done here it belongs in the follow-up PR alongside the module split, not in a bugfix PR.\n\n- hash: 03fc9aa5\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::mid_level_elegance::duplicate_unit_conversion_seam\n  verdict: exaggerated\n  verdict_reasoning: The duplication is real (config_publisher.py:119-120 and state_publisher.py:67-68 both call to_std_system on the same packet) but it is pure wasted work, not a defect. Verified to_std_system is idempotent \u2014 it rewrites usUnits from 1 to 17, so the second call is a no-op (once == twice) \u2014 and that it returns a NEW dict without mutating its argument, which is precisely what makes controller.py:288-293 safe when it hands one packet to two threads. No double-conversion error, no race.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Keep as a low-priority tidy (convert once in preprocessor_complete), but strip any implication of incorrectness. Note the idempotence finding in the item so nobody \"fixes\" a bug that is not there. Sequence after d5b8bef4, which touches the same two lines.\n\n- hash: 2dfb19b0\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::preprocessor_noop_init_and_unused_lambda_arg\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Split verdict. The no-op constructor is genuine and verbatim (preprocessor.py:23-25) \u2014 same as 6fb15215. The identity-lambda claim is genuine (see 35913ef6). The \"unused lambda parameter\" claim is real but should not be acted on (see 7574d120): all five registry entries take (x, cp) because state_publisher.py:86 and :119 invoke them through one uniform call shape.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/preprocessor.py, src/weewx_ha/utils.py, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py]\n  recommendation: Act on the __init__ and the identity lambda; drop the signature change. Merge the __init__ half into 6fb15215 and the lambda half into 35913ef6.\n\n- hash: da830555\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::low_level_elegance::redundant_none_guards_and_lazy_caches\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: The None-guard half is proven dead (see d5b8bef4 and 8473cc58) and is the in-scope part. The \"collapse the caches into one loaded-state object or functools.cache-based loaders\" half is the deferred locale redesign \u2014 and note that functools.cache specifically would make the inertness WORSE by hiding the cache behind a decorator, so that suggestion should not be adopted verbatim.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/utils.py, src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py]\n  recommendation: Take the guard deletions here (merge into d5b8bef4/8473cc58). Defer the cache restructuring and flag the functools.cache suggestion as rejected \u2014 the fix for the caches is an explicit reset hook (80ff170c), not more memoisation.\n\n- hash: c9bac941\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::implicit_global_locale_state\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Same problem as 91693263, verified by the same repro. Accurate: language and overrides are process-global (locale_loader.py:15, :18), set by Controller at :115/:125, and the downstream caches are never invalidated.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/locale_loader.py, src/weewx_ha/utils.py, src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Merge into the locale cluster. Its \"immutable Catalog injected into the publishers\" fix is the full redesign \u2014 defer that; the reset hook is the in-scope fix.\n\n- hash: 4910a237\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::abstraction_fitness::utils_global_lazy_caches\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Same problem as 91693263 from the abstraction_fitness angle; verified. The dependency it describes is exactly right: utils.py:15 imports the loaders, which read locale_loader's globals at call time (:151, :199), so utils' behaviour depends on Controller's call ORDER, not just its values.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/utils.py, src/weewx_ha/locale_loader.py]\n  recommendation: Merge into the locale cluster; defer the LocaleCatalog redesign.\n\n- hash: af356790\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::global_language_state_coordinates_modules\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Same problem as 91693263 from the cross_module angle; verified. Its fallback suggestion (\"at least provide a single reset function that clears the locale and utils caches together\") is the best-scoped statement of the in-scope fix in the entire cluster.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/locale_loader.py, src/weewx_ha/utils.py]\n  recommendation: Merge into the locale cluster and adopt its reset-function wording as the implementation.\n\n- hash: 80ff170c\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::locale_state_cache_not_invalidated\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Same problem as 91693263 from the initialization_coupling angle; verified. This is the entry that names the actionable remedy most precisely (a single utils.configure(language, overrides) that sets state and clears all four caches, called from Controller and used by tests).\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/utils.py, src/weewx_ha/locale_loader.py, src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Use as the canonical locale-cluster item; merge 91693263, af356790, c9bac941 and 4910a237 into it. Pair with b07d7c21, which cannot be fixed without it.\n\n## Import topology (one problem, eight entries)\n\n- hash: 69b906ae\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::cross_module_architecture::submodules_import_via_package_init\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Every piece of evidence verified line by line. __init__.py:8-9 carries \"isort is disabled below to prevent circular imports\" with a hand-ordered list (:11-17); controller.py:21 `from . import ConfigPublisher, PacketPreprocessor, StatePublisher`; state_publisher.py:10 `from . import ConfigPublisher, UnitSystem`; models/extension_config.py:10-11 `from . import MQTTConfig, StationInfo` and `from .. import UnitSystem`; models/__init__.py:3-10 has its own isort:off. The detector's independent 7-file cycle item corroborates it. The claim about config_publisher.py:160 is also right (see 9e1bb2fa).\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/__init__.py, src/weewx_ha/controller.py, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/models/__init__.py, src/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py, src/weewx_ha/models/mqtt_config.py]\n  recommendation: Canonical entry for the cluster. Genuine and the strongest finding in the set, but explicitly out of scope: defer to the follow-up PR with a note. Merge 8ef5f222, e89719a5, a9873b85, 13bd82d7, 58f43daf and 80587571 into it rather than carrying seven entries.\n\n- hash: 8ef5f222\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::high_level_elegance::package_self_import_and_order_dependence\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Identical problem to 69b906ae, verified from the same files. Adds nothing new.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/__init__.py, src/weewx_ha/controller.py, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py]\n  recommendation: Merge into 69b906ae.\n\n- hash: e89719a5\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::dependency_health::package_root_import_cycle\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Identical problem to 69b906ae, verified. Its \"then re-enable isort\" clause is accurate \u2014 both __init__.py and models/__init__.py carry isort:off/on pairs that exist only for this cycle.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/__init__.py, src/weewx_ha/models/__init__.py]\n  recommendation: Merge into 69b906ae.\n\n- hash: a9873b85\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::design_coherence::package_facade_import_cycle\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Identical problem to 69b906ae. Its \"7-file\" count matches the detector's cycle item exactly (__init__, config_publisher, controller, models/__init__, models/extension_config, state_publisher, utils).\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/__init__.py, src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Merge into 69b906ae.\n\n- hash: 13bd82d7\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::initialization_coupling::circular_import_order_dependency\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Identical problem to 69b906ae from the initialization_coupling angle; the \"hand-ordered import list\" claim is literally visible at __init__.py:11-17.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/__init__.py, src/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py]\n  recommendation: Merge into 69b906ae.\n\n- hash: 58f43daf\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::package_organization::models_imports_package_root\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Identical problem, but this is the BEST-SCOPED entry in the cluster and worth preserving for that reason. Its Stage 1 really is a single edit: extension_config.py:11 `from .. import UnitSystem` -> `from ..utils import UnitSystem`, which breaks the models<->root edge on its own. I confirmed utils.py does not import models, so that edit cannot create a new cycle.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py, src/weewx_ha/utils.py, src/weewx_ha/__init__.py]\n  recommendation: Merge into 69b906ae but carry its Stage 1 forward as the named first step of the deferred follow-up work, since it is independently safe and reviewable.\n\n- hash: 80587571\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::convention_outlier::mixed_intra_package_import_style\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: The mixed style is real and verifiable: config_publisher.py:12-14 imports siblings directly (`from ._version`, `from .models`, `from .utils`) while state_publisher.py:10 and controller.py:21 go through the package root. So the codebase already contains the target convention in one module and the legacy one in two.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Merge into 69b906ae. Worth noting in that item that config_publisher.py is the existing precedent for the fix.\n\n## Naming, conventions, typing\n\n- hash: 188c0f9e\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::naming_quality::process_packet_generic_verb\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Verified three process_packet methods with three return types (dict / bool / None) as described, and controller.py:288-293 submits two of them consecutively where only the callback name distinguishes them. The suggested names map correctly onto the actual behaviours.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/preprocessor.py, src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Canonical over bba009ae. Real, but renaming public methods touches both publishers, the controller and several tests \u2014 sequence it after the functional fixes, or defer with the module split.\n\n- hash: 0135cfb9\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::naming_quality::controller_callback_names_understate_effects\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Accurate. check_config_update does not merely check \u2014 it submits publish_discovery at controller.py:278. preprocessor_complete dispatches TWO follow-up tasks at :288 and :291. Both names describe a predicate or a notification while the bodies fan out work.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Low-value rename; these are private callbacks with no external callers, so it is cheap. Bundle with 97e41dcf, which rewrites the same submit sites anyway.\n\n- hash: abbb4b3a\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::naming_quality::key_config_unit_metadata_near_duplicate_names\n  verdict: not-worth-it\n  verdict_reasoning: The near-duplicate names are real (get_key_config/get_key_config_dict at utils.py:138/:257, get_unit_metadata/_get_unit_metadata_dict at :116/:44). But get_key_config and get_unit_metadata are both re-exported in __init__.py __all__ (:26-27), so renaming them is a public API break, and the proposed names (resolve_key_config, key_catalogue) are a matter of taste with no reader actually blocked. Classic YAGNI.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/utils.py, src/weewx_ha/__init__.py]\n  recommendation: Skip. If utils.py is ever split (9a621b48) the names can be reconsidered there for free.\n\n- hash: a5639216\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::naming_quality::camelcase_local_in_preprocessor\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Confirmed: preprocessor.py:32 binds a local `txBatteryStatus` in a module that is otherwise snake_case. Trivial, and the line is inside the exact block being rewritten for c5824dfd and 8ceb34bc.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/preprocessor.py]\n  recommendation: Rename to tx_battery_bitmap as part of the battery fix. Zero marginal cost there; do not raise a separate change for it.\n\n- hash: 421e119b\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::convention_outlier::stationinfo_validator_missing_classmethod\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Confirmed and correctly scoped as cosmetic. station_info.py:31-32 declares `@field_validator(\"time_zone\", mode=\"before\")` then `def validate_time_zone(cls, value)` with no @classmethod and no annotations, while both siblings do it properly (mqtt_config.py:36-38 and tls_config.py:41-43). I ran it: pydantic v2 handles it fine \u2014 valid zones parse, \"Not/AZone\" raises ValidationError, and no warning is emitted. So it is pure inconsistency, not a bug.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/models/station_info.py, src/weewx_ha/models/mqtt_config.py, src/weewx_ha/models/tls_config.py]\n  recommendation: Add @classmethod and annotations. One-line, zero risk \u2014 but note it is cosmetic, not a latent defect, so it should not outrank anything functional.\n\n- hash: ac394e82\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::convention_outlier::mixed_typing_idioms\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Confirmed. extension_config.py:5 `from typing import Any, Dict, Optional`, mqtt_config.py:4 `from typing import Optional`, tls_config.py:6 `from typing import Any, Optional`, versus PEP 604/585 throughout locale_loader.py (:15, :18) and utils.py (:20-22, :254). tls_config.py is half-migrated within one file: :19 uses Optional[str] while :43 already uses dict[str, Any].\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py, src/weewx_ha/models/mqtt_config.py, src/weewx_ha/models/tls_config.py, src/weewx_ha/locale_loader.py, src/weewx_ha/utils.py]\n  recommendation: Convert the three model files to `X | None` / `dict[...]`. Mechanical, confined to files the branch already touches. Duplicate of e4ac3e60 \u2014 carry once.\n\n- hash: e4ac3e60\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::type_safety::legacy_typing_half_migrated\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Same observation as ac394e82, verified across the same files; requires-python is >=3.10 (pyproject.toml:26) so both PEP 604 and PEP 585 are safe to use everywhere.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py, src/weewx_ha/models/mqtt_config.py, src/weewx_ha/models/tls_config.py, pyproject.toml]\n  recommendation: Canonical over ac394e82 (it names the concrete transformation). Merge the two.\n\n- hash: be27e802\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::type_safety::untyped_controller_callbacks\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Proven by mypy, not inferred. `mypy src` emits exactly: \"controller.py:272: note: By default the bodies of untyped functions are not checked [annotation-unchecked]\" and the same at :284 \u2014 i.e. check_config_update and preprocessor_complete bodies are SKIPPED. Also confirmed unannotated params on on_mqtt_connect (:202), on_mqtt_connect_fail (:222), on_mqtt_disconnect (:227), on_mqtt_message (:237), on_mqtt_subscribe (:250), on_mqtt_unsubscribe (:256), on_weewx_loop (:297) and on_weewx_archive (:309).\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Annotate them. High value for the cost: it is additive, touches only controller.py, and immediately puts two previously unchecked function bodies under mypy \u2014 which is where the shutDown/init defects live.\n\n- hash: 0cb58f9c\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::type_safety::bare_type_ignore\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Exact, and mypy-confirmed. Seven bare `# type: ignore` (controller.py:16, :17, :18, :19; config_publisher.py:10; utils.py:12, :13) versus one coded (`locale_loader.py:10 # type: ignore[import-untyped]`), and state_publisher.py:8 has NO ignore \u2014 which is the single error in the whole mypy run: \"state_publisher.py:8: error: Skipping analyzing 'weewx.units' ... [import-untyped]\". The finding's \"one import left unignored\" is literally the only mypy failure.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/controller.py, src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/utils.py, src/weewx_ha/locale_loader.py, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py]\n  recommendation: Add a `[[tool.mypy.overrides]] module = [\"weewx.*\", \"weeutil.*\"]` with ignore_missing_imports and drop the eight inline comments \u2014 one edit that fixes the mypy error AND the inconsistency. Prefer this over sprinkling `[import-untyped]` eight times.\n\n- hash: 5ce7dda5\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::type_safety::sensor_config_untyped_dict\n  verdict: over-engineering\n  verdict_reasoning: The description is accurate \u2014 key config really is dict[str, Any] with .get() access (utils.py:138, config_publisher.py:125-139, state_publisher.py:73-86). But a TypedDict cannot work here: the same dicts are user-extensible via ExtensionConfig.sensors/units/enums, which are declared `Optional[Dict[str, Any]]` (extension_config.py:40-54) and deep-merged from arbitrary user YAML (locale_loader.py:199-207), and the nested `metadata` carries arbitrary Home Assistant discovery keys. A total=False TypedDict permissive enough to accept that is nearly information-free, and it would touch utils, both publishers and the loader. The dict[str, float | None] half is also wrong \u2014 packets carry str and int values too (usUnits, dateTime).\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/utils.py, src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py, src/weewx_ha/locale_loader.py]\n  recommendation: Reject for this cycle with the user-extensibility reason recorded, so it is not re-proposed. If anything, type only the stable outer shape when utils.py is split.\n\n- hash: a79f3f42\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::error_consistency::minor_error_context_inconsistencies\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Observed directly in my repro output: the ValidationError is logged TWICE \u2014 once by extension_config.py:65 (\"Configuration validation error: ...\") and again by controller.py:105-108 (\"Invalid or missing extension configuration\", exc_info=True). Also confirmed extension_config.py:66 uses `raise e` instead of a bare `raise` (loses nothing here but is the non-idiomatic form the finding names) and controller.py:487 logs without exc_info while the five other handlers use it.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py, src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Log once at the controller boundary, use bare `raise`, add exc_info=True at :487. Small, and it lands in the same edit as the 9834b90a init fix.\n\n- hash: e297a66c\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::error_consistency::locale_load_failures_swallowed_dead_checks\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Both halves verified. load_yaml returns {} for a missing or malformed PACKAGED base file (locale_loader.py:161-166) \u2014 those files ship inside the wheel (pyproject.toml:50 package-data `locales/*.yaml`), so their absence is a packaging failure, not a runtime condition, and swallowing it degrades every sensor to guessed metadata silently. The dead RuntimeError checks are confirmed unexecuted by coverage (utils.py lines 40, 48, 56).\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/locale_loader.py, src/weewx_ha/utils.py, pyproject.toml]\n  recommendation: Canonical over afd54433. Raise for the base file with `from e`, keep the fallback only for the optional localized overlay, delete the three dead guards.\n\n## Dependencies, migration, tests\n\n- hash: e95b08a1\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::dependency_health::unused_runtime_setuptools\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Confirmed. pyproject.toml:19 lists setuptools in [project].dependencies, and grep finds no `import setuptools` or `pkg_resources` anywhere in src/ or tests/ (the only hits are in the generated src/weewx_home_assistant.egg-info/, which merely echoes the declaration). requirements.txt also lists `wheel`, which is likewise unused at runtime.\n  files_read: [pyproject.toml, requirements.txt, src/weewx_ha/utils.py]\n  recommendation: Drop setuptools from [project].dependencies and wheel from requirements.txt. Trivial and safe \u2014 version resolution uses `[tool.setuptools.dynamic] version = {attr = ...}`, which is build-time only.\n\n- hash: 448fddfa\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::dependency_health::weewx_unpinned_runtime\n  verdict: exaggerated\n  verdict_reasoning: The premise is right but the framing is misleading. weewx IS imported at runtime (utils.py:12-13, controller.py:16-19, config_publisher.py:10, state_publisher.py:8) and is NOT in [project].dependencies at all \u2014 it appears only as `weewx == 5.1.0` inside the test extra (pyproject.toml:40). But that is correct for a WeeWX extension: it is installed by `weectl extension install` into an existing WeeWX environment, so declaring weewx as a pip runtime dependency would be wrong and could pull a second copy. Only the documentation half of the suggestion is valid.\n  files_read: [pyproject.toml, src/weewx_ha/utils.py, src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Reduce to a docs item: state the supported WeeWX range in README. Explicitly reject adding weewx to [project].dependencies, and treat the paho-mqtt/pydantic upper-bound suggestion as optional.\n\n- hash: db656939\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::incomplete_migration::vestigial_time_zone_shim\n  verdict: exaggerated\n  verdict_reasoning: Partly already fixed by HEAD. Commit 12d9498 (\"drop the unused station time zone plumbing\") removed the consumers, and station_info.py:23-29 now documents the field as unused-but-still-accepted so existing configs keep validating \u2014 which is the right call and contradicts the finding's \"either drop it\" option. What genuinely remains: README.md:150 still advertises `timezone = <default: UTC>` as a normal configurable option with no hint that it is ignored, and three tests still pass it (test_discovery_race.py:50, test_publish.py:30, test_unit_groups.py:109).\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/models/station_info.py, README.md, tests/test_discovery_race.py, tests/test_publish.py, tests/test_unit_groups.py]\n  recommendation: Reduce to a README fix (mark `timezone` accepted-but-ignored). Do NOT drop the field \u2014 removal would break validation for existing user configs, which is exactly what the field's docstring preserves. Leave the test usages; they harmlessly exercise the compat path.\n\n- hash: 754dd47a\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::test_strategy::controller_event_paths_untested\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Strongly confirmed by coverage, every clause of it. controller.py is at 54% with __init__ (96-156), all six MQTT callbacks (205-247), the three future callbacks (263-295), on_weewx_loop (299-307), on_weewx_archive (318-342) and shutDown (477-491) all unexecuted. preprocessor.py is at 32% with 29-37 \u2014 the entire battery bitmask body \u2014 unexecuted, which is why c5824dfd and 8ceb34bc both went unnoticed. extension_config.py is at 77% with from_config_dict (61-66) unexecuted. TLSConfig is at 82%.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/controller.py, src/weewx_ha/preprocessor.py, src/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py, src/weewx_ha/models/tls_config.py, tests/test_mqtt_startup.py, tests/test_daily_sunshine.py]\n  recommendation: Highest-value test item, but per the plan's own rule it follows the code fixes. Start with the preprocessor tests that must accompany c5824dfd/8ceb34bc, then from_config_dict, then the shutDown-after-bad-config regression for 9834b90a.\n\n- hash: b07d7c21\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::test_strategy::duplicated_locale_reset_fixture\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Genuine and UNDERSTATED \u2014 the duplication is the lesser problem. Confirmed the fixture exists in six modules (test_hardening, test_locale_de, test_publish, test_locale_overrides, test_discovery_race, test_unit_groups) and that its docstring claims to \"Reset global locale state before and after each test\". But grep proves NO test anywhere touches _KEY_CONFIG, _SENSORS_YAML, _UNIT_METADATA or _ENUM_MAPS, and I verified set_language cannot reach them. The fixture is inert; it is harmless today only because every locale test calls locale_loader directly, bypassing utils' caches.\n  files_read: [tests/test_locale_de.py, tests/test_hardening.py, tests/test_publish.py, tests/test_locale_overrides.py, tests/test_discovery_race.py, tests/test_unit_groups.py, tests/conftest.py, src/weewx_ha/utils.py]\n  recommendation: Do NOT just move it to conftest \u2014 that would centralise a false guarantee. Depend it on 80ff170c: add the utils cache reset first, then move the (now truthful) autouse fixture into conftest.py, which is currently only pytest plumbing with no fixtures at all.\n\n- hash: d240d875\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::test_strategy::controller_tests_use_new_stubs\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Confirmed with exact sites. test_mqtt_startup.py:47 does `Controller.__new__(Controller)`. test_daily_sunshine.py:46-50 builds a SimpleNamespace and manually re-attaches `Controller._compute_event_rain` and `Controller._day_extreme` onto it, then :74 calls `Controller._augment_db_derived(_stub(mgr), record, filtered)` as an unbound function. The tests are coupled to three private names and to the engine.db_binder attribute path.\n  files_read: [tests/test_mqtt_startup.py, tests/test_daily_sunshine.py, src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Genuine, but the clean fix IS the deferred ArchiveAggregates extraction (0f87e46e) \u2014 extracting it gives these tests a public surface for free. Defer with that item rather than inventing a Controller factory fixture now.\n\n- hash: 7a286f22\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::test_strategy::no_cross_module_integration_test\n  verdict: genuine\n  verdict_reasoning: Confirmed. No test binds or fires NEW_LOOP_PACKET / NEW_ARCHIVE_RECORD; coverage shows on_weewx_loop (299-307) and on_weewx_archive (318-342) never execute, and the publishers are exercised only by calling process_packet directly (test_publish.py, test_discovery_race.py). So nothing verifies the preprocessor -> state/config publisher wiring that controller.py:288-295 sets up.\n  files_read: [tests/test_publish.py, tests/test_discovery_race.py, tests/test_daily_sunshine.py, src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Worth exactly one integration test (fake engine + mocked paho client, fire both events, assert discovery and state topics). Keep it to one \u2014 it is the cheapest check that would have caught the battery bug end to end. Sequence after the code fixes.\n\n- hash: 6ac7d0c1\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::ai_generated_debt::boilerplate_docstrings_and_entry_logs\n  verdict: exaggerated\n  verdict_reasoning: Real but much smaller than \"docstring bloat\" implies. The \"Parameters / None / Returns / None\" pattern appears in exactly TWO docstrings (config_publisher.py:197-204 and state_publisher.py:105-108), not pervasively. The entry-log claim is accurate at four sites: state_publisher.py:63, config_publisher.py:117, preprocessor.py:29 and :31. Most docstrings in the package are substantive and several (controller.py:27-43, :51-63, config_publisher.py:98-99, :136-139) carry genuinely valuable rationale that must NOT be trimmed.\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/preprocessor.py, src/weewx_ha/controller.py]\n  recommendation: Narrow to the two empty Parameters/Returns blocks and the four entry logs, with an explicit \"do not touch the rationale comments\" caveat. This is exactly the volume-over-value item the sense-check guidance warns about \u2014 keep it last.\n\n- hash: 7574d120\n  issue_id: review::.::holistic::abstraction_fitness::convert_lambda_unused_param\n  verdict: not-worth-it\n  verdict_reasoning: The observation is correct \u2014 all five _LAMBDA_REGISTRY entries (utils.py:215-223) take `(x, cp)` and none uses cp. But it is a deliberate uniform signature for a registry of callables, exactly as the STRATEGIZE guidance flags: state_publisher.py:86 and :119 both invoke `convert_lambda(value, self.config_publisher)` through one shape, and sensors.yaml references them by name so the arity is effectively a published contract. Changing it means editing 5 lambdas, 2 call sites, and the contract for any future converter that DOES need publisher context (e.g. a derived sensor reading sibling metadata).\n  files_read: [src/weewx_ha/utils.py, src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py, src/weewx_ha/locales/sensors.yaml]\n  recommendation: Skip, and record the \"uniform registry signature\" reason so it is not re-raised next cycle. Pair the skip note with the 2dfb19b0 and 050906d5 mentions of the same parameter.\n\n---\n\n- hash: ffffffffff\n  verdict: not-an-assessment\n  verdict_reasoning: Section terminator, not an issue assessment. Present so the\n    line-oriented template parser closes the preceding assessment block instead of\n    absorbing the cluster section's fields into it. Resolves to no issue and is discarded.\n  files_read: []\n  recommendation: Ignore this block.\n\n# Verdict tally\n\n- genuine: 53\n- false-positive: 1 (201b7680)\n- exaggerated: 7 (448fddfa, 9732236a, 03fc9aa5, 9c4a6940, ba9ac8fb, 6ac7d0c1, db656939)\n- over-engineering: 1 (5ce7dda5)\n- not-worth-it: 4 (abbb4b3a, 7574d120, 050906d5, d0256160)\n- total: 66\n\nOf the 53 genuine, only 11 are distinct problems once duplication is collapsed: the import cycle (8 entries), the locale caches (5), the half-initialised Controller (5), the controller/utils overload (5), the dead unit_system guard (3), the typing migration (2), the process_packet naming (2), the loader error contract (2), plus the battery bitmask, the None txBatteryStatus and the _augment_db_derived partial mutation.\n\nNothing was left unsettled. Every falsifiable claim in the set was either run or read to a conclusion; no finding required a judgement I could not ground in source lines, coverage output or mypy output.\n\n# Auto-cluster decisions\n\nAll 17 open detector items are unclustered singletons; I grouped them into six logical pseudo-clusters, sampled and read the cited lines for each, and render cluster-level verdicts. Every item is accounted for.\n\n- cluster: auto/dict_keys-phantom_read (2 items: config::integration, config::unitless)\n  verdict: mostly-false-positives\n  sample_count: 2\n  false_positive_rate: 1.0\n  recommendation: skip\n  reasoning: Both keys ARE written \u2014 just not in Python. `integration` appears 7 times and `unitless` 17 times in src/weewx_ha/locales/sensors.yaml (e.g. :23, :96, :106), loaded through locale_loader.load_sensors into _KEY_CONFIG and returned by get_key_config. The detector only traced the local `config` variable in config_publisher.py and could not see the YAML data source. config_publisher.py:129 and :174 are correct reads of real keys.\n\n- cluster: auto/cycles+facade (3 items: cycles 7-file, facade __init__.py, facade models/__init__.py)\n  verdict: actionable\n  sample_count: 3\n  false_positive_rate: 0.0\n  recommendation: defer\n  reasoning: The 7-file cycle is independently confirmed by my own read (__init__.py:8-19 isort:off, controller.py:21, state_publisher.py:10, models/extension_config.py:10-11) and is the same problem as review 69b906ae. The two facade items are accurate descriptions (32 LOC / 12 LOC re-export modules) and are the other side of the same coin. Fold all three into the 69b906ae item and defer to the follow-up PR per the scope boundary \u2014 do not promote separately.\n\n- cluster: auto/global_mutable_config (2 items: _current_language, _config_overrides)\n  verdict: actionable\n  sample_count: 2\n  false_positive_rate: 0.0\n  recommendation: defer\n  reasoning: Both accurate (locale_loader.py:15 and :18, each mutated from one site). They are the detector's view of the locale cluster whose real harm I reproduced. Fold into 80ff170c; the reset hook resolves them. No separate work.\n\n- cluster: auto/smells-genuine (4 items: controller::swallowed_error, controller::annotation_quality, preprocessor::annotation_quality, preprocessor::dead_function)\n  verdict: actionable\n  sample_count: 4\n  false_positive_rate: 0.0\n  recommendation: promote\n  reasoning: All four verified, and two are UNDERCOUNTED in the detector's favour. swallowed_error says 3x; there are 6 log-only except blocks (controller.py:104, 265, 273, 285, 413, 486). annotation_quality 9x in controller matches the mypy annotation-unchecked notes and the eight unannotated callbacks (= review be27e802). preprocessor annotation_quality is the bare `packet: dict` at :27. dead_function is the no-op __init__ at :23-25 (= review 6fb15215). Promote by folding into be27e802 and 6fb15215, both of which are already in scope.\n\n- cluster: auto/smells-false-positive (3 items: config_publisher::hardcoded_url, controller::magic_number, controller::todo_fixme)\n  verdict: mostly-false-positives\n  sample_count: 3\n  false_positive_rate: 0.67\n  recommendation: skip\n  reasoning: hardcoded_url is config_publisher.py:94 `\"support_url\": \"https://github.com/ThomDietrich/weewx-home-assistant\"` \u2014 a required field of the Home Assistant origin discovery payload, documented as such at :87-89. Not a smell. magic_number \"3x >1000 in logic\" is wrong: all four large values are named module constants with explanatory comments (controller.py:80-83 HOUR_S/DAY_S/RAIN_EVENT_GAP_S/RAIN_EVENT_LOOKBACK_S); the only bare literal is `3600.0` at :383, a seconds-to-hours conversion. todo_fixme is the single intentional roadmap note at controller.py:45; real but worthless to action.\n\n- cluster: auto/smells-structural (3 items: controller::structural large-file, locale_loader::high_cyclomatic_complexity, config_publisher::deferred_import)\n  verdict: mixed\n  sample_count: 3\n  false_positive_rate: 0.0\n  recommendation: break_up\n  reasoning: Three different fates, so they must not travel together. structural is exact (AST: Controller has 17 methods; 2 methods >50 LOC \u2014 __init__ at 68 and _augment_db_derived at 69) and belongs with the deferred 0f87e46e split. high_cyclomatic_complexity is accurate but UNDERCOUNTED (it reports 1x; both locale_loader._deep_merge at cc~15 and load_yaml at cc~17 exceed 12) \u2014 and both are not-worth-it: the complexity encodes documented behaviour (int-vs-str enum key reconciliation at :40-55, the three-layer priority load at :154-207) that a refactor would obscure, and load_yaml is at 85% coverage. deferred_import is config_publisher.py:160 and is the in-scope one-line fix already captured as review 9e1bb2fa \u2014 promote that one alone.\n\n---\n",
