        "enrich": {
          "stage": "enrich",
          "report": "# ENRICH \u2014 all 30 steps re-verified against source; 11 factual errors corrected\n\nEvery one of the 30 action steps was rewritten through `desloppify plan cluster update\n<name> --update-step N`. No attestation override was used. Each step was checked by opening\nthe file it names, confirming the cited line numbers, and \u2014 wherever the claim was\nfalsifiable \u2014 running it in the pipenv environment (`pipenv run pytest --cov=weewx_ha\n--cov-report=term-missing`, `pipenv run mypy src`, `pipenv run mypy --disallow-untyped-defs`,\nand direct Python probes against `weewx_ha.preprocessor`, `pydantic.Secret`,\n`datetime.fromtimestamp` and `weewx.units.to_std_system`).\n\n## Factual errors found and corrected (11)\n\n1. **controller-init-lifecycle-contract step 3 was not implementable.** It instructed the\n   executor to construct ConfigPublisher and StatePublisher *before*\n   `self.init_mqtt_client(...)` at controller.py:128. Both constructors take the mqtt client\n   as their first positional parameter (config_publisher.py:40-49,\n   state_publisher.py:34-40), and `init_mqtt_client` itself reads `self.availability_topic`\n   at :184. Rewritten as the fix that actually works: delete `client.loop_start()` at\n   controller.py:198 and call `self.mqtt_client.loop_start()` in `__init__` after the\n   StatePublisher construction ends at :152. Also recorded the consequence nobody had\n   noticed: `tests/test_mqtt_startup.py:55-60` asserts `loop_start` is in\n   `init_mqtt_client`'s call list and WILL FAIL; the step now says to move that assertion in\n   the same commit. Title changed to match.\n2. **dead-code-and-residue-deletion step 3 claimed a module-level twin that does not exist.**\n   The step said to delete the function-level `from .utils import get_key_config_dict` at\n   config_publisher.py:160 \"whose module-level twin sits at :14\". Line 14 is\n   `from .utils import UnitSystem, get_key_config, get_unit_metadata` \u2014 it does **not**\n   import `get_key_config_dict`. Deleting :160 alone produces a NameError at :166. The step\n   now instructs adding the name to the :14 import in the same edit, with the no-cycle proof\n   (utils.py imports only .locale_loader; __init__.py:12 imports utils before\n   config_publisher at :14).\n3. **timestamp-lambda-naming step 2 pointed at the wrong files.** `grep -c convert_lambda`\n   returns 0 for both sensors_cs.yaml and sensors_de.yaml \u2014 the localized catalogues contain\n   no convert_lambda keys at all. All nine references are in sensors.yaml (lines 18, 26, 166,\n   211, 226, 241, 715, 722, 730) and every one is `localtime_to_iso`.\n   `localtime_to_utc_timestamp` has **zero** YAML references; its only non-registry mention\n   is the docs line locales/README.md:134, which the step previously missed entirely and now\n   names, along with the gap that `localtime_to_iso` was never documented in that list\n   (README.md:132-135).\n4. **controller-callback-typing-and-submit step 3 miscounted and mislocated.** It said\n   \"eight unannotated callbacks\" at :221, :225, :236, :252, :257, :261, :270, :298.\n   `pipenv run mypy --disallow-untyped-defs src/weewx_ha/controller.py` gives the real set:\n   **nine** \u2014 the six MQTT handlers at :201, :222, :226, :237, :249, :255 and the three\n   future callbacks at :261, :268, :281 (plus the two WeeWX event handlers at :297 and :309).\n   The \"two unchecked bodies\" claim is confirmed and now pinned to the exact mypy output\n   lines, controller.py:272 and :284.\n5. **controller-callback-typing-and-submit step 2 cited definition lines that are not\n   definitions.** `check_config_update` is defined at :268, not :270; `preprocessor_complete`\n   at :281, not \":298 and :337\" (those two lines are inside `on_weewx_loop` and\n   `on_weewx_archive`). The three reference sites it gave (:295, :305, :340) were correct and\n   are kept; the docstrings at :269 and :282 were added, since they repeat the bad names.\n6. **controller-init-lifecycle-contract step 2 named a non-existent attribute.** The\n   attribute is `packet_preprocessor` (assigned at controller.py:134), not `preprocessor`.\n   `self.config` (:101) was also missing from the list although `on_mqtt_connect` reads\n   `self.config.discovery_topic_prefix` at :211 and `on_mqtt_message` at :242.\n7. **docstring-and-entry-log-trim step 1 double-counted.** It claimed \"four entry-only debug\n   logs in config_publisher.py and state_publisher.py\", then said two of them are deleted by\n   cluster 1 \u2014 but those two are preprocessor.py:29 and :31, a third file. There are exactly\n   **two** in the named files: config_publisher.py:117 and state_publisher.py:63. The two\n   empty docstring blocks are now pinned exactly: config_publisher.py:198-204 and\n   state_publisher.py:106-108 (not :105-108).\n8. **locale-cache-invalidation step 2 had the Controller block off by two.** The real range\n   is controller.py:114-125 (set_language at :115, overrides dict at :118-124,\n   set_config_overrides at :125), not :116-126.\n9. **coverage-gaps step 1 over-claimed.** `from_config_dict` is declared at\n   extension_config.py:56-66 but only the **body**, :61-66, is uncovered; the decorator and\n   signature execute at import. Coverage puts the file at 77% with `61-66` missing.\n10. **controller-init-lifecycle-contract step 4 cited :106 for a call that starts at :105.**\n    The `logger.error(...)` spans controller.py:105-108. Also added that\n    extension_config.py's module `logger` (:13) has no other user once :65 goes.\n11. **timestamp-lambda-naming step 1 called the lambda a \"verified mathematical identity\"\n    without qualification.** Measured: it *is* an exact identity for every integer epoch \u2014\n    which is what a WeeWX `dateTime` is \u2014 but for fractional inputs it round-trips through\n    datetime's microsecond resolution (169,304 of 200,000 random floats changed; largest\n    deviation 5.1e-07 s). The verdict (drop the entry) stands; the step now states the real\n    property instead of an overstated one.\n\n## Claims verified as correct, then sharpened with the proof\n\n- **The battery fix is right.** `(bitmask >> i) & 1` was exercised over all 256 bitmaps and\n  all eight fields: it yields only 0 or 1 in every case. Measured current output for bitmap\n  255 is `batteryStatusISS=1` then 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128 \u2014 so 7 of 8 fields are broken,\n  and the step's \"channels 1 through 7, not channels 2-7\" correction is right. The catalogue\n  side is confirmed: `payload_off: 0` / `payload_on: 1` at sensors.yaml:95-103\n  (`batteryStatusChannel`, which channels 1..7 reach through the numeric-suffix fallback at\n  utils.py:150-157) and :105-113 (`batteryStatusISS`). The `del packet[\"txBatteryStatus\"]`\n  requirement is confirmed necessary and currently violated: the None bitmask raises\n  `TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for &: 'NoneType' and 'int'` at preprocessor.py:35,\n  i.e. **before** the `del` at :36, so the key survives and the whole packet is dropped by\n  `preprocessor_complete`'s handler at controller.py:286. All of that is now in the step.\n- **The dead `unit_system` guards.** DELETE confirmed on five proofs, the fifth measured:\n  coverage reports partial branches `119->121` (config_publisher.py) and `67->69`\n  (state_publisher.py) \u2014 the None arm of each is never taken. `to_std_system` was also\n  re-measured as returning a new dict and being idempotent, so the settled \"double conversion\n  is safe\" verdict holds.\n- **The three RuntimeError guards** at utils.py:39-40, :47-48, :55-56 are exactly where\n  claimed, and coverage lists lines 40, 48 and 56 as unexecuted.\n- **The mypy override works.** Verified with `mypy --config-file <probe>`: a bare\n  `[[tool.mypy.overrides]]` table is honoured even with no `[tool.mypy]` section (the repo has\n  no mypy config at all \u2014 no mypy.ini, no setup.cfg), and it takes `mypy src` from 1 error to\n  \"Success: no issues found in 13 source files\". A probe with `warn_unused_ignores = true`\n  confirms the seven redundant ignores are exactly controller.py:16-19,\n  config_publisher.py:10 and utils.py:12-13 \u2014 and that locale_loader.py:10 is correctly\n  excluded (it is for yaml, and the override does not cover it).\n- **The seven `executor.submit` sites** (:217-218, :246-247, :278-279, :288-290, :291-295,\n  :302-305, :337-340) are confirmed \u2014 seven, not five. Added the fact that makes the helper\n  design non-obvious: three distinct callbacks are in use, so `_submit` must accept one.\n- **controller.py sits at exactly 54%**, with the full missing-line list now recorded.\n- **The six duplicated `reset_locale_state` fixtures** are confirmed at test_locale_de.py:24,\n  test_locale_overrides.py:21, test_hardening.py:12, test_discovery_race.py:32,\n  test_publish.py:19, test_unit_groups.py:68 \u2014 byte-identical, and none can reach the utils\n  caches. Added the detail the step needed to be mechanical: they are **not** autouse, so 22\n  test functions and one `publisher` fixture also lose a parameter.\n- **README.md:150** is confirmed as the `timezone = <default: UTC>` line in the `[[station]]`\n  block at :146-150, and **utils.py:150-190** (the key-guessing fallback) is confirmed at\n  zero coverage, with `get_key_config` returning a dict on all three exits (:147, :157, :190)\n  \u2014 so the predicted TypeError at config_publisher.py:125 cannot occur. The rejection stands.\n- **StationInfo's validator** is purely cosmetic: it works today and pydantic emits no warning\n  for the plain-function form. Recorded so the executor does not treat it as a defect.\n\n## Executor-readiness gaps closed\n\nBeyond the corrections, 23 of the 30 steps carried **no `src/`-rooted file path** that the\nvalidator's path extractor can see \u2014 they named bare filenames like `utils.py:39-40`. All 30\nnow carry at least one verified `src/...` path, and every path in every detail resolves on\ndisk. Every step names the file, the line range, the exact edit, and (for the test steps) the\nassertions and the command that proves the current failure. Each of the six \"add a test\" steps\nnow says what the test asserts and which existing test module to put it in.\n\n## The not-yet-existing test file\n\n`tests/test_preprocessor.py` does not exist. The validator's extractor is\n`(?:[\\w./-]+/)?(?:src|supabase)/[\\w./-]+\\.\\w+(?::\\d+...)?` \u2014 it only matches paths rooted at\n`src/` or `supabase/`, so `tests/`-rooted paths are never extracted and never\nexistence-checked (the same is true of `README.md`, `pyproject.toml` and `requirements.txt`,\nwhich several steps name). Verified by running the extractor over all 30 details: zero bad\npaths. So the step keeps the name and states the truth plainly \u2014 \"Create\ntests/test_preprocessor.py \u2014 no such file exists today; tests/ holds ten modules and none of\nthem touches src/weewx_ha/preprocessor.py\" \u2014 while the step's validator-visible path is the\nreal `src/weewx_ha/preprocessor.py`. Nothing is phrased as if the file already existed.\n\n## Settled decisions preserved verbatim\n\nEvery rejection carried in from organize is still in the step details and none was reopened:\ndelete rather than harden the `unit_system` guards; `to_std_system` is idempotent so the\ndouble conversion is safe; the `get_key_config` returns-None claim is rejected while its\nzero-coverage test survives; `StationInfo.time_zone` stays and only README.md:150 is\ncorrected; weewx must not become a pip runtime dependency; `load_yaml` is untouched in this\nPR; `functools.cache` and the injected-catalogue redesign are refused; the `convert_lambda`\narity change is refused; the stale \"use HOUR_S\" and `/ 3600.0` clauses must not be acted on;\nlocale_loader.py:10's coded yaml ignore stays.\n\n## Scope\n\nNo repository source file was modified \u2014 this stage produced plan state only. All 42 clustered\nissue IDs are still referenced, each generated from plan.json rather than typed; no step\nreferences any of the 24 skipped issues. Dry run is clean: \"All steps have detail or\nissue_refs\", zero bad-path warnings, zero missing-effort notes.\n",
