        "sense-check": {
          "stage": "sense-check",
          "report": "# SENSE-CHECK \u2014 three independent passes, merged by the orchestrator\n\nThree checks ran in parallel and reported to me; I recorded this stage myself so three\nagents would not write to plan.json at once. Content and structure each attacked the\nenrich pass's own claims; the value check was told explicitly to argue for less. I\nre-verified the two findings that reverse an earlier decision (below) against the\nrunning code before accepting them.\n\nThe headline: **the plan was carrying too much, and one \"settled, measured\" decision\nwas wrong.** PR #1 goes from 12 clusters / 30 steps to 6 clusters / 12 steps. Everything\ncut is deferred, not dropped.\n\n## The two findings that reverse earlier stages\n\n### 1. The three RuntimeError cache guards are NOT dead code \u2014 they do type work\n`dead-code-and-residue-deletion` step 2 was to delete the guards at\nsrc/weewx_ha/utils.py:39-40, :47-48 and :55-56, justified by coverage showing those\nbranches never execute. Coverage was right about runtime and silent about purpose.\nMeasured, by copying src/ to a scratch tree, removing exactly those three blocks and\nrunning the repo's own mypy against it:\n\n    utils.py:39: error: Incompatible return value type (got \"dict[str, dict[int, str]] | None\", expected \"dict[str, dict[int, str]]\")  [return-value]\n    utils.py:45: error: Incompatible return value type (got \"dict[str, dict[str, Any]] | None\", expected \"dict[str, dict[str, Any]]\")  [return-value]\n    utils.py:51: error: Incompatible return value type (got \"dict[str, Any] | None\", expected \"dict[str, Any]\")  [return-value]\n\nBaseline on the real tree is 1 error (src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py:8). So the step\nadds three. The guards narrow `X | None` to `X` for the three public getters\nget_enum_maps, _get_unit_metadata_dict and get_sensors_yaml, whose module globals\n(_ENUM_MAPS, _UNIT_METADATA, _SENSORS_YAML, declared at utils.py:20-22 and assigned in\n_ensure_loaded at :25-33) are Optional. Step dropped.\n\nTwo welcome consequences. The mypy-weewx-import-overrides cluster claimed it would reach\n\"Success: no issues found\"; that claim rested on this step and is now moot, which is part\nof why that cluster is deferred. And the deferred `defer-to-followup-pr/error-contract`\ngroup stays genuinely standalone: the structure check had found that deleting these\nguards would silently pre-commit one of the two directions that follow-up is supposed to\nchoose between. Not deleting them removes the trap.\n\n### 2. Renaming the timestamp lambdas is a user-visible breaking change\n`timestamp-lambda-naming` renames `localtime_to_iso` and drops\n`localtime_to_utc_timestamp` from _LAMBDA_REGISTRY at src/weewx_ha/utils.py:214-224.\nThose names are not internal: `convert_lambda:` is catalogue vocabulary, and\nsrc/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py:40-42 exposes a `sensors` option described as\n\"Override sensor configurations from sensors.yaml\", merged over the packaged catalogue.\n_build_key_config at utils.py:236-248 resolves a `convert_lambda` name against the\nregistry and, on a miss, logs a warning and **deletes the key**. A user whose own\nconfiguration references the old name therefore gets a raw Unix epoch published to Home\nAssistant instead of an ISO timestamp, announced only by one line in the log. That is the\nsame class of change as the `load_yaml` raise already deferred for this reason. It needs a\ndeprecation alias and its own PR. Deferred.\n\n## Decision Ledger\n\n- preprocessor-battery-bitmap \u2014 **keep**. Both steps earn their place: two of the four reproduced defects. Verified src/weewx_ha/preprocessor.py:29-37 (the `txBatteryStatus & (1 << i)` fan-out, 0% covered) against src/weewx_ha/locales/sensors.yaml:95-113, where `batteryStatusChannel` and `batteryStatusISS` both declare payload_on 1 / payload_off 0.\n- controller-init-lifecycle-contract \u2014 **tighten**. Keep steps 1, 2 and 4; drop step 3. Steps 1-2 fix the AttributeError from the early return at src/weewx_ha/controller.py:105-109 reaching `shutDown` at :480. Step 3 (moving `loop_start()` out of `init_mqtt_client` at :198) fixes no defect, changes MQTT start-up ordering in the one function that already needed an incident fix for felddy/weewx-home-assistant#74, invalidates tests/test_mqtt_startup.py:55-60, and buys only the deletion of two `getattr` probes at :216 and :244. Step 2 must annotate the disabled-path attribute as `mqtt.Client | None` to stay mypy-clean against the declaration at :128.\n- locale-cache-invalidation \u2014 **tighten**. The inert setters are the fourth defect, so the cluster stays. Step 2 shrinks: invalidate from inside the existing `set_language` / `set_config_overrides` at src/weewx_ha/locale_loader.py:70 and :96 via one private reset in src/weewx_ha/utils.py, rather than adding a new public `configure()` and rewriting the Controller call sites at controller.py:114-125. Step 3 keeps the conftest move with two corrections the content check measured: 19 test functions plus the `publisher` fixture lose the parameter, not 22, and the now-unused imports in tests/test_hardening.py, tests/test_discovery_race.py, tests/test_publish.py and tests/test_unit_groups.py must go or flake8 F401 fires.\n- archive-derived-atomic-update \u2014 **skip** to the follow-up PR. Not among the reproduced defects. Its step 1 claims nothing covers `_augment_db_derived`, which is false: tests/test_daily_sunshine.py:53-116 holds three passing tests of it with a reusable `_FakeManager` and `_stub`. Its step 2 would table-drive src/weewx_ha/controller.py:346-414 and, if the table is reached through `self`, those three tests fail silently because the outer `except Exception` swallows the AttributeError.\n- controller-callback-typing-and-submit \u2014 **skip** to the follow-up PR. All three steps are structure and polish in the most-reviewed file, which this cycle's split rule sends to the follow-up. Steps 1 and 2 also conflict: step 1 rewrites the very call sites at controller.py:295, :305 and :340 whose line numbers step 2 then cites.\n- dead-code-and-residue-deletion \u2014 **tighten**. Keep step 1 (the two unreachable `unit_system is not None` guards at src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py:119 and src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py:67, proven dead five ways including partial-branch coverage) and step 3's duplicated local import at config_publisher.py:160, which must add `get_key_config_dict` to the module import at :14 in the same edit or the file raises NameError at :166. Drop step 2 for the mypy reason above.\n- timestamp-lambda-naming \u2014 **skip** to the follow-up PR, for the breaking-change reason above.\n- mypy-weewx-import-overrides \u2014 **skip** to the follow-up PR, as one packaging-and-config chore with the deferred dependency steps. It adds a `[[tool.mypy.overrides]]` table to pyproject.toml and clears seven inline ignores at src/weewx_ha/controller.py:16-19, src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py:10 and src/weewx_ha/utils.py:12-13. Safe, but not a defect fix, and its clean-mypy claim depended on the step just dropped.\n- coverage-gaps-controller-and-catalogue \u2014 **tighten**. Keep step 1 only, covering `ExtensionConfig.from_config_dict` at src/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py:57-66, whose failure path the lifecycle fix exercises; its assertion needs correcting, because lifecycle step 4 deletes the only `logger.error` inside that method at :65, so the count there becomes zero and the surviving log is the Controller's at controller.py:105-108. Defer step 2 (new fake-engine integration harness, tests none of the four defects) and step 3 (the catalogue guessing fallback at src/weewx_ha/utils.py:150-190, unrelated to the defects).\n- dependency-and-readme-hygiene \u2014 **tighten**. Keep step 3 only: README.md:150 still advertises the `timezone` key that commit 12d9498 on this branch removed the plumbing for, so this one line completes work already here. Defer steps 1 and 2 (pyproject.toml:19 and requirements.txt:3 metadata, README.md:65-66 version range) into the packaging chore.\n- models-typing-and-validator \u2014 **skip** to the follow-up PR. Cosmetic typing idiom across src/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py, mqtt_config.py, tls_config.py and station_info.py, changing no behaviour. The missing `from e` on `raise ValueError` at station_info.py:39, which the content check found belongs to nobody, travels with it.\n- docstring-and-entry-log-trim \u2014 **skip** to the follow-up PR. Two `logger.debug` lines at src/weewx_ha/config_publisher.py:117 and src/weewx_ha/state_publisher.py:63 plus two empty docstring blocks. A one-issue cluster saving two lines, and theme-only rather than file-local.\n\n## Corrections to the follow-up PR manifest\n\n- **The cut-point advice was backwards.** The manifest said to cut the follow-up branch before `models-typing-and-validator` lands. Cutting early guarantees conflicts, because module-decomposition extracts src/weewx_ha/controller.py:346-414 and the utils.py split collides with everything PR #1 does in that file. Cut the follow-up *after* PR #1 merges, then rebase.\n- **The named merge-conflict surface was the wrong one.** It is not the import block of src/weewx_ha/models/extension_config.py, where the hunks sit 2 and 6 lines apart and merge cleanly. It is the import block of src/weewx_ha/controller.py:16-24, which import-topology rewrites at :22 while locale-cache rewrites :24 and the deferred mypy chore edits :16-19.\n- The deferred `api-naming` and `controller_tests_use_new_stubs` groups now have fewer new consumers to migrate, because the `_submit` helper and the integration harness are deferred alongside them.\n- `error-contract` is standalone again, per finding 1.\n\n## Structural notes applied without changing a verdict\n\nThe graph is acyclic and the recorded order is a valid topological sort. Of the declared\ndependency edges, five carry real semantics (5\u21922, 6\u21923, 9\u21921, 9\u21922, 11\u21922) and the rest only\npreserved line-number citations; with six clusters deferred most of the spurious edges\nleave with them. Two cascade gaps must be honoured by whoever executes: dropping the\nlocale setters' direct calls leaves the import at src/weewx_ha/controller.py:24 unused\n(flake8 F401), and the comment block at controller.py:186-197 explains why the host is set\nbefore the network thread starts, so it stays exactly as it is now that step 3 is dropped.\nAll citations are against current HEAD and clusters edit the same files in sequence, so\nexecutors locate code by name, not by line number.\n\n## What PR #1 now carries\n\nSix clusters, twelve steps: the battery fan-out fix and its test; the disabled-Controller\nlifecycle fix, its test and the duplicate-log tidy; the locale cache invalidation, its test\nand the conftest dedup; the two dead `unit_system` guards and the duplicated local import;\nthe `from_config_dict` coverage test; and the one-line README correction. Four reproduced\ndefects, the tests that fail without their fixes, and nothing a reviewer has to take on\ntrust.\n",
