          "confirmed_text": "I merged three independent sense-check passes (content, structure, value) and recorded the stage myself so they would not write to plan.json concurrently. I re-verified the two findings that reverse earlier stages before accepting them: removing the three RuntimeError guards from utils.py adds three mypy return-value errors against a baseline of one, so they are type-narrowing rather than dead code and dead-code-and-residue-deletion step 2 is dropped; and the _LAMBDA_REGISTRY names are user-facing convert_lambda vocabulary reachable through the sensors override option, so timestamp-lambda-naming is a silent breaking change and is deferred. The ledger covers all twelve clusters exactly once: preprocessor-battery-bitmap keep; controller-init-lifecycle-contract, locale-cache-invalidation, dead-code-and-residue-deletion, coverage-gaps-controller-and-catalogue and dependency-and-readme-hygiene tighten; archive-derived-atomic-update, controller-callback-typing-and-submit, timestamp-lambda-naming, mypy-weewx-import-overrides, models-typing-and-validator and docstring-and-entry-log-trim skipped to the follow-up PR. PR #1 drops from 30 steps to 12."
        }
      },
      "strategy": "Fix the four reproduced defects first, each behind a test verified to fail against the current code, then take only the cleanups that live in files those fixes already touch. Order: the txBatteryStatus fan-out in preprocessor.py, where 7 of 8 battery sensors publish 2..128 against payload_on 1 and can never report low, together with the None-bitmask TypeError that silently drops the whole packet; the disabled Controller, whose early return at controller.py:109 leaves mqtt_client unset for shutDown at :480; the locale caches in utils.py, which make set_language inert and the six duplicated reset fixtures a false guarantee; then the two genuinely dead unit_system guards, the duplicated local import, one from_config_dict coverage test, and the README line that commit 12d9498 left stale. Everything structural is deferred to a follow-up PR in six groups -- import-topology, module-decomposition, api-naming, packaging-and-config, typing-idiom and error-contract -- cut AFTER this PR merges and then rebased, because module-decomposition rewrites the same controller.py and utils.py regions this PR touches. Two earlier conclusions were reversed on evidence and must not be reopened: the three RuntimeError guards in utils.py are type-narrowing, not dead, since removing them adds three mypy return-value errors against a baseline of one; and renaming the _LAMBDA_REGISTRY timestamp entries is a user-visible breaking change, because convert_lambda names are catalogue vocabulary users can reference through the sensors override and an unknown name degrades to publishing a raw epoch with only a log warning. The plan deliberately carries 12 steps across 6 clusters, not 30 across 12: a reviewer should be able to check four defect fixes and their tests without taking anything on trust.",
